e expedition that first successfully reached the North Pole in 1926 was special."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (ongoing state)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "With 타다 it shows a continuing state: 타고 있었어요 = was on board.", "ex_ko": "비행선에는 유명한 탐험가 로알드 아문센이 타고 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The famous explorer Roald Amundsen was aboard the airship."}, {"name": "~과/와 (with/and)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "with / and (formal)", "ex_ko": "이탈리아 엔지니어와 미국 부자, 그리고 폭스 테리어 개 한 마리도 함께했어요.", "ex_en": "An Italian engineer, a wealthy American, and even a fox terrier came along too."}, {"name": "~도 (also)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "inclusive. \"also / too\"", "ex_ko": "이탈리아 엔지니어와 미국 부자, 그리고 폭스 테리어 개 한 마리도 함께했어요.", "ex_en": "An Italian engineer, a wealthy American, and even a fox terrier came along too."}, {"name": "~적으로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a Sino-Korean noun into an adverb: 성공 → 성공적 (successful) → 성공적으로 (successfully).", "ex_ko": "탐험대는 북극점에 성공적으로 도달했어요.", "ex_en": "The expedition team successfully reached the North Pole."}, {"name": "~지 못하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''could not V''. 오래가다 (to last long) → 오래가지 못했어요 (did not last long).", "ex_ko": "하지만 승리의 기쁨은 오래가지 못했어요.", "ex_en": "However, the joy of victory did not last long."}, {"name": "~ 때문에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "because of (noun)", "ex_ko": "문제는 국기 때문에 시작되었어요.", "ex_en": "The problem started because of the flag."}, {"name": "~보다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "comparative particle (than)", "ex_ko": "이탈리아 국기가 다른 나라 국기들보다 크게 만들어져 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The Italian flag had been made larger than the flags of other countries."}, {"name": "~게", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "adverbializer suffix", "ex_ko": "이탈리아 국기가 다른 나라 국기들보다 크게 만들어져 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The Italian flag had been made larger than the flags of other countries."}, {"name": "~아/어져 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Passive + resulting state: 만들다 → 만들어지다 (to be made) → 만들어져 있었어요 (had been made).", "ex_ko": "이탈리아 국기가 다른 나라 국기들보다 크게 만들어져 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The Italian flag had been made larger than the flags of other countries."}, {"name": "~(으)로 인해", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "due to/because of", "ex_ko": "이로 인해 탐험대원들 사이에 큰 논란이 벌어졌어요.", "ex_en": "Due to this, a big controversy arose among the expedition members."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp1uel65if9z' and md5(translation) = '2f3b4411e6a2bea93cf69b3543948268';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["The Mona Lisa is the most famous painting in the world. However, for a long time it was not known who the woman in this painting was.", "In 2005, a German researcher made an important discovery. He found a handwritten memo in the margin of an old book.", "In this memo, it was written that Leonardo da Vinci was painting a portrait of Lisa del Giocondo in 1503. This memo was confirmed to be genuine.", "In this way, it was finally discovered who the Mona Lisa is. Lisa del Giocondo was the wife of an Italian merchant."], "sentences": [{"text": "모나리자는 세계에서 가장 유명한 그림이에요.", "translation": "The Mona Lisa is the most famous painting in the world.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세계", "en": "world", "note": "noun; 세계에서 = ''in the world''"}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous", "note": "adjective; 유명한 is the modifier form"}, {"ko": "그림", "en": "painting / drawing / picture", "note": "noun"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. 모나리자 + 는 → 모나리자는 (''as for the Mona Lisa''). Used because 모나리자 ends in a vowel.", "example_in_sentence": "모나리자는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "Location-of-action particle. 세계 + 에서 → 세계에서 (''in the world'').", "example_in_sentence": "세계에서"}]}, {"text": "하지만 이 그림 속 여성이 누구인지는 오랫동안 알려지지 않았어요.", "translation": "However, for a long time it was not known who the woman in this painting was.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여성", "en": "woman / female", "note": "noun; formal/neutral term"}, {"ko": "오랫동안", "en": "for a long time", "note": "adverb; 오래 + 동안 combined"}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to become known / to be known", "note": "passive of 알리다 (to inform)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만 (but)", "exp": "Contrast conjunction. 하다 → 하지만 (''but / however''); here used as a sentence-initial connective.", "example_in_sentence": "하지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle. 여성 + 이 → 여성이 (''the woman [is the subject]''). Used because 여성 ends in a consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "여성이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic/contrastive particle. 누구인지 + 는 → 누구인지는 (''as for who [she] is''). Marks the embedded clause as the topic.", "example_in_sentence": "누구인지는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Long-form negation. 알려지다 → 알려지지 않다 → 알려지지 않았어요 (''was not known'').", "example_in_sentence": "알려지지 않았어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 않다 → 않았어요; stem 않 has vowel ㅏ → 았어요 (''was not'').", "example_in_sentence": "않았어요"}]}, {"text": "2005년에 독일 연구자가 중요한 발견을 했어요.", "translation": "In 2005, a German researcher made an important discovery.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연구자", "en": "researcher", "note": "noun; 연구 (research) + 자 (person)"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "adjective; 중요한 is the modifier form"}, {"ko": "발견", "en": "discovery / finding", "note": "noun; 발견하다 = to discover"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "Time particle. 2005년 + 에 → 2005년에 (''in the year 2005'').", "example_in_sentence": "2005년에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle. 연구자 + 가 → 연구자가 (''a researcher [did]''). Used because 연구자 ends in a vowel.", "example_in_sentence": "연구자가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 발견 + 을 → 발견을 (''a discovery [as object]''). Used because 발견 ends in a consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "발견을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "했어요 (하다 past polite)", "exp": "하다 verb past polite. 하다 → 했어요 (''did / made''). 발견을 하다 = to make a discovery.", "example_in_sentence": "했어요"}]}, {"text": "그는 오래된 책의 여백에서 손으로 쓴 메모를 찾았어요.", "translation": "He found a handwritten memo in the margin of an old book.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old / to be aged", "note": "verb; 오래된 is the past modifier form meaning ''old''"}, {"ko": "여백", "en": "margin / blank space", "note": "noun; 여백에서 = ''in the margin''"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find / to look for", "note": "verb; context here means ''to find''"}, {"ko": "메모", "en": "memo / note", "note": "noun; loanword from English ''memo''"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. 그 + 는 → 그는 (''he [as topic]''). Used because 그 ends in a vowel.", "example_in_sentence": "그는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Possessive/attributive particle. 책 + 의 → 책의 (''of the book / the book''s'').", "example_in_sentence": "책의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "Location-of-action particle. 여백 + 에서 → 여백에서 (''in the margin'').", "example_in_sentence": "여백에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (means/direction)", "exp": "Instrument/means particle. 손 + 으로 → 손으로 (''by hand / with the hand''). Used because 손 ends in a consonant (ㄴ).", "example_in_sentence": "손으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 메모 + 를 → 메모를 (''the memo [as object]''). Used because 메모 ends in a vowel.", "example_in_sentence": "메모를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 찾다 → 찾 + 았어요 → 찾았어요 (''found''). Stem vowel ㅏ → 았.", "example_in_sentence": "찾았어요"}]}, {"text": "이 메모에는 레오나르도 다 빈치가 1503년에 리사 델 지오콘도의 초상화를 그리고 있다고 적혀 있었어요.", "translation": "In this memo, it was written that Leonardo da Vinci was painting a portrait of Lisa del Giocondo in 1503.", "vocab": [{"ko": "초상화", "en": "portrait", "note": "noun; 초상 (portrait) + 화 (painting)"}, {"ko": "그리다", "en": "to draw / to paint", "note": "verb; 그리고 있다 = ''is painting''"}, {"ko": "적히다", "en": "to be written / to be noted", "note": "passive of 적다 (to write/note down)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "에 (in) + 는 (topic): 메모 → 메모에는 (''in this memo'').", "example_in_sentence": "메모에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle. 레오나르도 다 빈치 + 가 → 레오나르도 다 빈치가 (''Leonardo da Vinci [as subject]''). Ends in vowel → 가.", "example_in_sentence": "레오나르도 다 빈치가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "Time particle. 1503년 + 에 → 1503년에 (''in the year 1503'').", "example_in_sentence": "1503년에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Possessive particle. 리사 델 지오콘도 + 의 → 리사 델 지오콘도의 (''of Lisa del Giocondo'').", "example_in_sentence": "리사 델 지오콘도의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 초상화 + 를 → 초상화를 (''the portrait [as object]''). Ends in vowel → 를.", "example_in_sentence": "초상화를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "Progressive aspect. 그리다 → 그리 + 고 있다 → 그리고 있다 (''is painting''). Embedded in a quoted clause here.", "example_in_sentence": "그리고 있다고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 있다 → 있 + 었어요 → 있었어요 (''was [written]''). Stem vowel not ㅏ/ㅗ → 었.", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 메모는 진짜임이 확인되었어요.", "translation": "This memo was confirmed to be genuine.", "vocab": [{"ko": "진짜", "en": "real / genuine / true", "note": "noun/adverb; 진짜임 = ''the fact of being genuine'' (nominalised)"}, {"ko": "확인되다", "en": "to be confirmed / to be verified", "note": "passive of 확인하다 (to confirm)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. 메모 + 는 → 메모는 (''this memo [as topic]''). Ends in vowel → 는.", "example_in_sentence": "메모는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle. 진짜임 + 이 → 진짜임이 (''the fact of being genuine [as subject]''). Ends in consonant → 이.", "example_in_sentence": "진짜임이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 되다 → 되 + 었어요 → 됐어요 (contracted) / 되었어요 (''was confirmed''). Here written in full form 되었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "확인되었어요"}]}, {"text": "이렇게 해서 모나리자가 누구인지 마침내 알게 되었어요.", "translation": "In this way, people finally learned who the Mona Lisa was.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이렇게", "en": "in this way / like this", "note": "adverb; 이렇다 → 이렇게"}, {"ko": "마침내", "en": "finally / at last", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "알다", "en": "to know / to come to know", "note": "verb; 알게 되다 = ''come to know''"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle. 모나리자 + 가 → 모나리자가 (''the Mona Lisa [as subject]''). Ends in vowel → 가.", "example_in_sentence": "모나리자가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (cause / sequence)", "exp": "Sequence/reason connector. 하다 → 해서 (''and so / by doing this''). 이렇게 해서 = ''by doing it this way / in this way''.", "example_in_sentence": "이렇게 해서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다 (come to / passive)", "exp": "Circumstance change pattern. 알다 → 알 + 게 되다 → 알게 되었어요 (''came to know / it came about that [we] knew'').", "example_in_sentence": "알게 되었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 되다 → 되 + 었어요 → 되었어요 (''came to be / it became so''). Stem vowel not ㅏ/ㅗ → 었.", "example_in_sentence": "되었어요"}]}, {"text": "리사 델 지오콘도는 이탈리아 상인의 아내였어요.", "translation": "Lisa del Giocondo was the wife of an Italian merchant.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상인", "en": "merchant / trader", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": "noun; refers to one''s own or another''s wife"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. 리사 델 지오콘도 + 는 → 리사 델 지오콘도는 (''as for Lisa del Giocondo''). Ends in vowel → 는.", "example_in_sentence": "리사 델 지오콘도는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Possessive particle. 상인 + 의 → 상인의 (''of the merchant / the merchant''s'').", "example_in_sentence": "상인의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 이다 → 이었어요 → contracted to 였어요 (''was''). 아내 + 였어요 → 아내였어요 (''was [the] wife'').", "example_in_sentence": "아내였어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "세계", "en": "world", "note": "noun; 세계에서 = ''in the world''"}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous", "note": "adjective; 유명한 is the modifier form"}, {"ko": "그림", "en": "painting / drawing / picture", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "여성", "en": "woman / female", "note": "noun; formal/neutral term"}, {"ko": "오랫동안", "en": "for a long time", "note": "adverb; 오래 + 동안 combined"}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to become known / to be known", "note": "passive of 알리다 (to inform)"}, {"ko": "연구자", "en": "researcher", "note": "noun; 연구 (research) + 자 (person)"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": "adjective; 중요한 is the modifier form"}, {"ko": "발견", "en": "discovery / finding", "note": "noun; 발견하다 = to discover"}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old / to be aged", "note": "verb; 오래된 is the past modifier form meaning ''old''"}, {"ko": "여백", "en": "margin / blank space", "note": "noun; 여백에서 = ''in the margin''"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find / to look for", "note": "verb; context here means ''to find''"}, {"ko": "메모", "en": "memo / note", "note": "noun; loanword from English ''memo''"}, {"ko": "초상화", "en": "portrait", "note": "noun; 초상 (portrait) + 화 (painting)"}, {"ko": "그리다", "en": "to draw / to paint", "note": "verb; 그리고 있다 = ''is painting''"}, {"ko": "적히다", "en": "to be written / to be noted", "note": "passive of 적다 (to write/note down)"}, {"ko": "진짜", "en": "real / genuine / true", "note": "noun/adverb; 진짜임 = ''the fact of being genuine'' (nominalised)"}, {"ko": "확인되다", "en": "to be confirmed / to be verified", "note": "passive of 확인하다 (to confirm)"}, {"ko": "이렇게", "en": "in this way / like this", "note": "adverb; 이렇다 → 이렇게"}, {"ko": "마침내", "en": "finally / at last", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "알다", "en": "to know / to come to know", "note": "verb; 알게 되다 = ''come to know''"}, {"ko": "상인", "en": "merchant / trader", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": "noun; refers to one''s own or another''s wife"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic/contrastive particle. 누구인지 + 는 → 누구인지는 (''as for who [she] is''). Marks the embedded clause as the topic.", "ex_ko": "모나리자는 세계에서 가장 유명한 그림이에요.", "ex_en": "The Mona Lisa is the most famous painting in the world."}, {"name": "~에서 (location/source)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Location-of-action particle. 여백 + 에서 → 여백에서 (''in the margin'').", "ex_ko": "모나리자는 세계에서 가장 유명한 그림이에요.", "ex_en": "The Mona Lisa is the most famous painting in the world."}, {"name": "~지만 (but)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Contrast conjunction. 하다 → 하지만 (''but / however''); here used as a sentence-initial connective.", "ex_ko": "하지만 이 그림 속 여성이 누구인지는 오랫동안 알려지지 않았어요.", "ex_en": "However, for a long time it was not known who the woman in this painting was."}, {"name": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Subject particle. 레오나르도 다 빈치 + 가 → 레오나르도 다 빈치가 (''Leonardo da Vinci [as subject]''). Ends in vowel → 가.", "ex_ko": "하지만 이 그림 속 여성이 누구인지는 오랫동안 알려지지 않았어요.", "ex_en": "However, for a long time it was not known who the woman in this painting was."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Long-form negation. 알려지다 → 알려지지 않다 → 알려지지 않았어요 (''was not known'').", "ex_ko": "하지만 이 그림 속 여성이 누구인지는 오랫동안 알려지지 않았어요.", "ex_en": "However, for a long time it was not known who the woman in this painting was."}, {"name": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past polite ending. 되다 → 되 + 었어요 → 됐어요 (contracted) / 되었어요 (''was confirmed''). Here written in full form 되었어요.", "ex_ko": "하지만 이 그림 속 여성이 누구인지는 오랫동안 알려지지 않았어요.", "ex_en": "However, for a long time it was not known who the woman in this painting was."}, {"name": "~을/를 (object marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Direct object particle. 발견 + 을 → 발견을 (''a discovery [as object]''). Used because 발견 ends in a consonant.", "ex_ko": "2005년에 독일 연구자가 중요한 발견을 했어요.", "ex_en": "In 2005, a German researcher made an important discovery."}, {"name": "했어요 (하다 past polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "하다 verb past polite. 하다 → 했어요 (''did / made''). 발견을 하다 = to make a discovery.", "ex_ko": "2005년에 독일 연구자가 중요한 발견을 했어요.", "ex_en": "In 2005, a German researcher made an important discovery."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possessive/attributive particle. 책 + 의 → 책의 (''of the book / the book''s'').", "ex_ko": "그는 오래된 책의 여백에서 손으로 쓴 메모를 찾았어요.", "ex_en": "He found a handwritten memo in the margin of an old book."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (means/direction)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Instrument/means particle. 손 + 으로 → 손으로 (''by hand / with the hand''). Used because 손 ends in a consonant (ㄴ).", "ex_ko": "그는 오래된 책의 여백에서 손으로 쓴 메모를 찾았어요.", "ex_en": "He found a handwritten memo in the margin of an old book."}, {"name": "~에는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "에 (in) + 는 (topic): 메모 → 메모에는 (''in this memo'').", "ex_ko": "이 메모에는 레오나르도 다 빈치가 1503년에 리사 델 지오콘도의 초상화를 그리고 있다고 적혀 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In this memo, it was written that Leonardo da Vinci was painting a portrait of Lisa del Giocondo in 1503."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive aspect. 그리다 → 그리 + 고 있다 → 그리고 있다 (''is painting''). Embedded in a quoted clause here.", "ex_ko": "이 메모에는 레오나르도 다 빈치가 1503년에 리사 델 지오콘도의 초상화를 그리고 있다고 적혀 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In this memo, it was written that Leonardo da Vinci was painting a portrait of Lisa del Giocondo in 1503."}, {"name": "~아/어서 (cause / sequence)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Sequence/reason connector. 하다 → 해서 (''and so / by doing this''). 이렇게 해서 = ''by doing it this way / in this way''.", "ex_ko": "이렇게 해서 모나리자가 누구인지 마침내 알게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "In this way, people finally learned who the Mona Lisa was."}, {"name": "~게 되다 (come to / passive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Circumstance change pattern. 알다 → 알 + 게 되다 → 알게 되었어요 (''came to know / it came about that [we] knew'').", "ex_ko": "이렇게 해서 모나리자가 누구인지 마침내 알게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "In this way, people finally learned who the Mona Lisa was."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp1ufuf158ch' and md5(translation) = 'b920ac5e9b25f04ea66cfae6a13b55d2';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Spencer Perceval is the only British Prime Minister to have been assassinated in history. In 1812, he was shot to death inside Parliament. Something remarkable happened. People who were outside Parliament heard the news of the assassination and were delighted. They tried to shake hands with the assassin. Soldiers came out and stopped the people. It was because too many people had gathered. The trial proceeded very quickly in court. The assassin was tried within 4 days. And he was executed a week later.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "스펜서 퍼시벌은 영국 역사상 암살당한 유일한 총리입니다.", "translation": "Spencer Perceval is the only prime minister in British history who was assassinated.", "vocab": [{"ko": "암살당하다", "en": "to be assassinated"}, {"ko": "유일하다", "en": "to be the only one"}, {"ko": "총리", "en": "prime minister"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "Topic-marking particle. Introduces the subject of the sentence.", "example_in_sentence": "스펜서 퍼시벌은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs: 암살당하다 (to be assassinated) → 암살당한 총리 (a prime minister who was assassinated).", "example_in_sentence": "암살당한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~입니다", "exp": "Formal declarative ending. Asserts a fact in polite formal style.", "example_in_sentence": "총리입니다"}]}, {"text": "1812년에 그는 국회의사당 안에서 총에 맞아 죽었어요.", "translation": "In 1812, he was shot and died inside the parliament building.", "vocab": [{"ko": "국회의사당", "en": "parliament building"}, {"ko": "총에 맞다", "en": "to be shot"}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle indicating the location where an action takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "안에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 (connective ending)", "exp": "Connects two sequential actions. Here: 맞다 → 맞아, then 죽다 (shot, then died).", "example_in_sentence": "맞아 죽었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense informal polite ending. Indicates completed action. 죽다 → 죽었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "죽었어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "총에 맞다", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning to be shot. Literally: hit by a gun.", "example_in_sentence": "총에 맞아"}]}, {"text": "놀라운 일이 일어났어요.", "translation": "Something surprising happened.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "ㅂ irregular + ~(으)ㄴ modifier", "exp": "놀랍다 (to be surprising): ㅂ becomes 우 before -은 → 놀라운 일 (a surprising thing).", "example_in_sentence": "놀라운"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense informal polite ending. 일어나다 → 일어났어요.", "example_in_sentence": "일어났어요"}]}, {"text": "국회의사당 밖에 있던 사람들이 암살 소식을 듣고 기뻐했습니다.", "translation": "People who were outside the parliament building heard the assassination news and were delighted.", "vocab": [{"ko": "밖", "en": "outside"}, {"ko": "소식", "en": "news"}, {"ko": "기뻐하다", "en": "to be delighted; to rejoice"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~던 (past descriptive form)", "exp": "Describes a past habitual or continuous state. 있다 → 있던 (people who were [there]).", "example_in_sentence": "있던"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (connective ending)", "exp": "Connects two actions in sequence. Here: 듣다 → 듣고, then 기뻐하다 (heard and then rejoiced).", "example_in_sentence": "듣고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었습니다", "exp": "Past tense formal declarative ending. 기뻐하다 → 기뻐했습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "기뻐했습니다"}]}, {"text": "그들은 암살범과 악수하려고 했어요.", "translation": "They tried to shake hands with the assassin.", "vocab": [{"ko": "암살범", "en": "assassin"}, {"ko": "악수하다", "en": "to shake hands"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "Comitative particle meaning ''with'' or ''and''. Marks the co-participant.", "example_in_sentence": "암살범과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~려고 하다", "exp": "Expresses intention or attempt to do something. 악수하다 → 악수하려고 했어요 (tried to shake hands).", "example_in_sentence": "악수하려고 했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense informal polite ending. Marks completed attempt.", "example_in_sentence": "했어요"}]}, {"text": "군인들이 나와서 사람들을 막았습니다.", "translation": "Soldiers came out and stopped the people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "군인", "en": "soldier"}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to come out"}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to stop; to block"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (connective ending)", "exp": "Connects two sequential actions with causal or temporal relation. 나오다 → 나와서, then 막다 (came out, then stopped).", "example_in_sentence": "나와서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었습니다", "exp": "Past tense formal declarative ending. 막다 → 막았습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "막았습니다"}]}, {"text": "사람들이 너무 많이 몰려들었기 때문이에요.", "translation": "It was because too many people gathered together.", "vocab": [{"ko": "몰려들다", "en": "to gather; to crowd together"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "Expresses reason or cause. Nominalizes the verb and marks reason. 몰려들다 → 몰려들었기 때문.", "example_in_sentence": "몰려들었기 때문이에요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었", "exp": "Past tense form within the nominalized clause. 몰려들다 → 몰려들었기.", "example_in_sentence": "몰려들었기"}]}, {"text": "법정에서 재판이 매우 빨리 진행되었어요.", "translation": "The trial proceeded very quickly in court.", "vocab": [{"ko": "법정", "en": "court; courtroom"}, {"ko": "재판", "en": "trial"}, {"ko": "진행되다", "en": "to proceed; to progress"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle indicating location where action takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "법정에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense informal polite ending. 진행되다 → 진행되었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "진행되었어요"}]}, {"text": "암살범은 4일 만에 재판을 받았습니다.", "translation": "The assassin received a trial in just 4 days.", "vocab": [{"ko": "재판을 받다", "en": "to receive/undergo a trial"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "Topic-marking particle introducing the subject.", "example_in_sentence": "암살범은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 만에", "exp": "''after / within (a span of time)''. 4일 만에 = only four days later.", "example_in_sentence": "4일 만에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었습니다", "exp": "Past tense formal declarative ending. 받다 → 받았습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "받았습니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "재판을 받다", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning to undergo/receive a trial.", "example_in_sentence": "재판을 받았습니다"}]}, {"text": "그리고 일주일 후에 처형당했어요.", "translation": "And a week later, he was executed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "처형당하다", "en": "to be executed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Temporal particle marking a point in time. 일주일 후에 (a week later).", "example_in_sentence": "후에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense informal polite ending. 처형당하다 → 처형당했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "처형당했어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "암살당하다", "en": "to be assassinated", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유일하다", "en": "to be the only one", "note": ""}, {"ko": "총리", "en": "prime minister", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국회의사당", "en": "parliament building", "note": ""}, {"ko": "총에 맞다", "en": "to be shot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밖", "en": "outside", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소식", "en": "news", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기뻐하다", "en": "to be delighted; to rejoice", "note": ""}, {"ko": "암살범", "en": "assassin", "note": ""}, {"ko": "악수하다", "en": "to shake hands", "note": ""}, {"ko": "군인", "en": "soldier", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to come out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to stop; to block", "note": ""}, {"ko": "몰려들다", "en": "to gather; to crowd together", "note": ""}, {"ko": "법정", "en": "court; courtroom", "note": ""}, {"ko": "재판", "en": "trial", "note": ""}, {"ko": "진행되다", "en": "to proceed; to progress", "note": ""}, {"ko": "재판을 받다", "en": "to receive/undergo a trial", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처형당하다", "en": "to be executed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영국", "en": "Britain, United Kingdom", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역사상", "en": "in history, historically", "note": ""}, {"ko": "총", "en": "gun", "note": ""}, {"ko": "맞다", "en": "to be hit, to get shot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing, matter, event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to be, exist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person, people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "암살", "en": "assassination", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그들", "en": "they, them", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do", "note": ""}, {"ko": "너무", "en": "too much, very", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "a lot, much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very, extremely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빨리", "en": "quickly, fast", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그리고", "en": "and, then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일주일", "en": "one week", "note": ""}, {"ko": "후", "en": "after, later", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~은/는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic-marking particle. Introduces the subject of the sentence.", "ex_ko": "스펜서 퍼시벌은 영국 역사상 암살당한 유일한 총리입니다.", "ex_en": "Spencer Perceval is the only prime minister in British history who was assassinated."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs: 암살당하다 (to be assassinated) → 암살당한 총리 (a prime minister who was assassinated).", "ex_ko": "스펜서 퍼시벌은 영국 역사상 암살당한 유일한 총리입니다.", "ex_en": "Spencer Perceval is the only prime minister in British history who was assassinated."}, {"name": "~입니다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Formal declarative ending. Asserts a fact in polite formal style.", "ex_ko": "스펜서 퍼시벌은 영국 역사상 암살당한 유일한 총리입니다.", "ex_en": "Spencer Perceval is the only prime minister in British history who was assassinated."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle indicating the location where an action takes place.", "ex_ko": "1812년에 그는 국회의사당 안에서 총에 맞아 죽었어요.", "ex_en": "In 1812, he was shot and died inside the parliament building."}, {"name": "~아/어서 (connective ending)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connects two sequential actions with causal or temporal relation. 나오다 → 나와서, then 막다 (came out, then stopped).", "ex_ko": "1812년에 그는 국회의사당 안에서 총에 맞아 죽었어요.", "ex_en": "In 1812, he was shot and died inside the parliament building."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense informal polite ending. Indicates completed action. 죽다 → 죽었어요.", "ex_ko": "1812년에 그는 국회의사당 안에서 총에 맞아 죽었어요.", "ex_en": "In 1812, he was shot and died inside the parliament building."}, {"name": "ㅂ irregular + ~(으)ㄴ modifier", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "놀랍다 (to be surprising): ㅂ becomes 우 before -은 → 놀라운 일 (a surprising thing).", "ex_ko": "놀라운 일이 일어났어요.", "ex_en": "Something surprising happened."}, {"name": "~던 (past descriptive form)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes a past habitual or continuous state. 있다 → 있던 (people who were [there]).", "ex_ko": "국회의사당 밖에 있던 사람들이 암살 소식을 듣고 기뻐했습니다.", "ex_en": "People who were outside the parliament building heard the assassination news and were delighted."}, {"name": "~고 (connective ending)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connects two actions in sequence. Here: 듣다 → 듣고, then 기뻐하다 (heard and then rejoiced).", "ex_ko": "국회의사당 밖에 있던 사람들이 암살 소식을 듣고 기뻐했습니다.", "ex_en": "People who were outside the parliament building heard the assassination news and were delighted."}, {"name": "~았/었습니다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense formal declarative ending. 기뻐하다 → 기뻐했습니다.", "ex_ko": "국회의사당 밖에 있던 사람들이 암살 소식을 듣고 기뻐했습니다.", "ex_en": "People who were outside the parliament building heard the assassination news and were delighted."}, {"name": "~과/와", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Comitative particle meaning ''with'' or ''and''. Marks the co-participant.", "ex_ko": "그들은 암살범과 악수하려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "They tried to shake hands with the assassin."}, {"name": "~려고 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Expresses intention or attempt to do something. 악수하다 → 악수하려고 했어요 (tried to shake hands).", "ex_ko": "그들은 암살범과 악수하려고 했어요.", "ex_en": "They tried to shake hands with the assassin."}, {"name": "~기 때문이다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Expresses reason or cause. Nominalizes the verb and marks reason. 몰려들다 → 몰려들었기 때문.", "ex_ko": "사람들이 너무 많이 몰려들었기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "It was because too many people gathered together."}, {"name": "~았/었", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense form within the nominalized clause. 몰려들다 → 몰려들었기.", "ex_ko": "사람들이 너무 많이 몰려들었기 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "It was because too many people gathered together."}, {"name": "~ 만에", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "''after / within (a span of time)''. 4일 만에 = only four days later.", "ex_ko": "암살범은 4일 만에 재판을 받았습니다.", "ex_en": "The assassin received a trial in just 4 days."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp1uh2zzfpmg' and md5(translation) = '51256c179f58a897a7ef430042a8633c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["President John F. Kennedy suffered from severe chronic back pain for several years. President John F. Kennedy suffered from severe chronic back pain for several years. This pain had a significant impact on his daily life.", "Kennedy underwent a total of four surgeries to resolve his back problems. The surgeries included disk removal and spinal fusion procedures. He also received two minor surgeries.", "However, despite all these numerous surgeries, Kennedy''s pain continued. The surgeries were not able to completely resolve his back problems.", "President Kennedy carried out his presidential duties despite bearing such physical pain. He tried to overcome his health problems."], "sentences": [{"text": "존 F.", "translation": "John F.", "vocab": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "케네디 대통령은 수년 동안 심각한 만성 허리 통증으로 고생했습니다.", "translation": "President John F. Kennedy suffered from severe chronic back pain for several years.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고생하다", "en": "to suffer, to have a hard time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "심각하다", "en": "to be serious, severe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만성", "en": "chronic", "note": "medical term"}, {"ko": "통증", "en": "pain", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "past formal-polite (vowel-contracted form). 고생하다 → 고생했습니다", "example_in_sentence": "고생했습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 고생하다", "exp": "''to suffer from N''; (으)로 marks the cause: 허리 통증으로 고생했습니다 = suffered from back pain.", "example_in_sentence": "통증으로 고생했습니다"}]}, {"text": "이 통증은 그의 일상생활에 큰 영향을 미쳤어요.", "translation": "This pain had a significant impact on his daily life.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일상생활", "en": "daily life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영향", "en": "influence, impact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "미치다", "en": "to have an effect, to influence", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past polite (vowel-contracted form). 미치다 → 미쳤어요", "example_in_sentence": "미쳤어요"}]}, {"text": "케네디는 허리 문제를 해결하기 위해 총 네 번의 수술을 받았습니다.", "translation": "Kennedy underwent a total of four surgeries to resolve his back problems.", "vocab": [{"ko": "해결하다", "en": "to solve, to resolve", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수술", "en": "surgery, operation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "past formal-polite ending. 받다 → 받았습니다", "example_in_sentence": "받았습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해(서) (in order to)", "exp": "purpose. \"in order to / for the sake of\". 해결하다 → 해결하기 위해", "example_in_sentence": "해결하기 위해"}]}, {"text": "수술에는 디스크 제거술과 척추 유합술이 포함되었어요.", "translation": "The surgeries included disk removal and spinal fusion procedures.", "vocab": [{"ko": "제거술", "en": "removal surgery", "note": "medical term"}, {"ko": "척추", "en": "spine, vertebrae", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유합술", "en": "fusion surgery", "note": "medical term"}, {"ko": "포함되다", "en": "to be included", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past polite ending. 포함되다 → 포함되었어요", "example_in_sentence": "포함되었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 (with/and)", "exp": "with / and (formal). 제거술과 척추 유합술 (disk removal and spinal fusion)", "example_in_sentence": "제거술과"}]}, {"text": "또한 두 번의 작은 수술도 받았습니다.", "translation": "He also received two minor surgeries.", "vocab": [{"ko": "또한", "en": "also, in addition", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "past formal-polite ending. 받다 → 받았습니다", "example_in_sentence": "받았습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also)", "exp": "inclusive. \"also / too\". 수술도 (surgery too/also)", "example_in_sentence": "수술도"}]}, {"text": "하지만 이런 많은 수술에도 불구하고 케네디의 통증은 계속되었습니다.", "translation": "However, despite all these numerous surgeries, Kennedy''s pain continued.", "vocab": [{"ko": "계속되다", "en": "to continue", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "past formal-polite ending. 계속되다 → 계속되었습니다", "example_in_sentence": "계속되었습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만 (but)", "exp": "contrast. \"but / however\". 하다 → 하지만", "example_in_sentence": "하지만"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에도 불구하고 (despite)", "exp": "concession. \"despite / in spite of\". 수술에도 불구하고 (despite the surgeries)", "example_in_sentence": "수술에도 불구하고"}]}, {"text": "수술들이 그의 허리 문제를 완전히 해결하지는 못했어요.", "translation": "The surgeries were not able to completely resolve his back problems.", "vocab": [{"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지는 못하다", "exp": "''could not (fully) V''; 는 adds contrast: 해결하다 → 해결하지는 못했어요 (did not completely solve it).", "example_in_sentence": "해결하지는 못했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past polite (vowel-contracted form). 못하다 → 못했어요", "example_in_sentence": "못했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~히 (adverb suffix, Sino-Korean)", "exp": "adverbializer for Sino-Korean and a few native bases. 완전하다 → 완전히 (completely)", "example_in_sentence": "완전히"}]}, {"text": "케네디 대통령은 이러한 신체적 고통을 안고도 대통령직을 수행했습니다.", "translation": "President Kennedy carried out his presidential duties despite bearing such physical pain.", "vocab": [{"ko": "신체적", "en": "physical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고통", "en": "pain, suffering", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안다", "en": "to hold, to carry", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수행하다", "en": "to perform, to carry out", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "past formal-polite (vowel-contracted form). 수행하다 → 수행했습니다", "example_in_sentence": "수행했습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고도 / ~면서도 (despite)", "exp": "despite doing / while still being. 안다 → 안고도 (despite carrying)", "example_in_sentence": "안고도"}]}, {"text": "그는 자신의 건강 문제를 극복하려고 노력했어요.", "translation": "He tried to overcome his health problems.", "vocab": [{"ko": "극복하다", "en": "to overcome", "note": ""}, {"ko": "노력하다", "en": "to make an effort, to try hard", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "past polite (vowel-contracted form). 노력하다 → 노력했어요", "example_in_sentence": "노력했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 (intention)", "exp": "in order to / intending to. 극복하다 → 극복하려고", "example_in_sentence": "극복하려고"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "고생하다", "en": "to suffer, to have a hard time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "심각하다", "en": "to be serious, severe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만성", "en": "chronic", "note": "medical term"}, {"ko": "통증", "en": "pain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일상생활", "en": "daily life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영향", "en": "influence, impact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "미치다", "en": "to have an effect, to influence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해결하다", "en": "to solve, to resolve", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수술", "en": "surgery, operation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제거술", "en": "removal surgery", "note": "medical term"}, {"ko": "척추", "en": "spine, vertebrae", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유합술", "en": "fusion surgery", "note": "medical term"}, {"ko": "포함되다", "en": "to be included", "note": ""}, {"ko": "또한", "en": "also, in addition", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속되다", "en": "to continue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신체적", "en": "physical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고통", "en": "pain, suffering", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안다", "en": "to hold, to carry", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수행하다", "en": "to perform, to carry out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "극복하다", "en": "to overcome", "note": ""}, {"ko": "노력하다", "en": "to make an effort, to try hard", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "past formal-polite (vowel-contracted form). 고생하다 → 고생했습니다", "ex_ko": "케네디 대통령은 수년 동안 심각한 만성 허리 통증으로 고생했습니다.", "ex_en": "President John F. Kennedy suffered from severe chronic back pain for several years."}, {"name": "~(으)로 고생하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''to suffer from N''; (으)로 marks the cause: 허리 통증으로 고생했습니다 = suffered from back pain.", "ex_ko": "케네디 대통령은 수년 동안 심각한 만성 허리 통증으로 고생했습니다.", "ex_en": "President John F. Kennedy suffered from severe chronic back pain for several years."}, {"name": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "past polite (vowel-contracted form). 노력하다 → 노력했어요", "ex_ko": "이 통증은 그의 일상생활에 큰 영향을 미쳤어요.", "ex_en": "This pain had a significant impact on his daily life."}, {"name": "~기 위해(서) (in order to)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "purpose. \"in order to / for the sake of\". 해결하다 → 해결하기 위해", "ex_ko": "케네디는 허리 문제를 해결하기 위해 총 네 번의 수술을 받았습니다.", "ex_en": "Kennedy underwent a total of four surgeries to resolve his back problems."}, {"name": "~과/와 (with/and)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "with / and (formal). 제거술과 척추 유합술 (disk removal and spinal fusion)", "ex_ko": "수술에는 디스크 제거술과 척추 유합술이 포함되었어요.", "ex_en": "The surgeries included disk removal and spinal fusion procedures."}, {"name": "~도 (also)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "inclusive. \"also / too\". 수술도 (surgery too/also)", "ex_ko": "또한 두 번의 작은 수술도 받았습니다.", "ex_en": "He also received two minor surgeries."}, {"name": "~지만 (but)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "contrast. \"but / however\". 하다 → 하지만", "ex_ko": "하지만 이런 많은 수술에도 불구하고 케네디의 통증은 계속되었습니다.", "ex_en": "However, despite all these numerous surgeries, Kennedy''s pain continued."}, {"name": "~지는 못하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''could not (fully) V''; 는 adds contrast: 해결하다 → 해결하지는 못했어요 (did not completely solve it).", "ex_ko": "수술들이 그의 허리 문제를 완전히 해결하지는 못했어요.", "ex_en": "The surgeries were not able to completely resolve his back problems."}, {"name": "~히 (adverb suffix, Sino-Korean)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "adverbializer for Sino-Korean and a few native bases. 완전하다 → 완전히 (completely)", "ex_ko": "수술들이 그의 허리 문제를 완전히 해결하지는 못했어요.", "ex_en": "The surgeries were not able to completely resolve his back problems."}, {"name": "~고도 / ~면서도 (despite)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "despite doing / while still being. 안다 → 안고도 (despite carrying)", "ex_ko": "케네디 대통령은 이러한 신체적 고통을 안고도 대통령직을 수행했습니다.", "ex_en": "President Kennedy carried out his presidential duties despite bearing such physical pain."}, {"name": "~(으)려고 (intention)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "in order to / intending to. 극복하다 → 극복하려고", "ex_ko": "그는 자신의 건강 문제를 극복하려고 노력했어요.", "ex_en": "He tried to overcome his health problems."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp1ui888zwor' and md5(translation) = 'c25368c66a03350e3b6288d8d428db7b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Purple is rarely seen in national flags. This is because purple dyes were historically very expensive.", "In the past, making purple dye was extremely difficult. Purple could only be obtained from sea snails living in the Mediterranean Sea.", "One pound of purple dye cost $56,000 in today''s money. This was an incredibly expensive price.", "Now purple dye is made artificially. So the price has become much cheaper."], "sentences": [{"text": "보라색은 국기에서 거의 보이지 않아요.", "translation": "Purple is rarely seen in national flags.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보라색", "en": "purple", "note": "color"}, {"ko": "국기", "en": "national flag", "note": "country''s flag"}, {"ko": "거의", "en": "almost, hardly", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to be seen, to appear", "note": "passive of 보다 (to see)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Makes a verb negative: 보이다 (to be seen) → 보이지 않다 (not be seen).", "example_in_sentence": "보이지 않아요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending: 않다 → 않아요.", "example_in_sentence": "보이지 않아요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "location particle indicating where action takes place. 국기에서 = in/on flags", "example_in_sentence": "국기에서"}]}, {"text": "그 이유는 보라색 물감의 비싼 값 때문이에요.", "translation": "The reason is the high price of purple dye.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": "cause"}, {"ko": "물감", "en": "paint, dye", "note": "coloring material"}, {"ko": "비싸다", "en": "to be expensive", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "값", "en": "price, cost", "note": "money value"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. 이유는 = as for the reason", "example_in_sentence": "이유는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive/modifier particle. 보라색 물감의 값 = purple dye''s price", "example_in_sentence": "물감의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 때문이에요", "exp": "''It is because of N''. 비싼 값 때문이에요 = it is because of the high price.", "example_in_sentence": "값 때문이에요"}]}, {"text": "옛날에는 보라색 물감을 만들기가 매우 어려웠어요.", "translation": "In the past, making purple dye was extremely difficult.", "vocab": [{"ko": "옛날", "en": "old times, the past", "note": "long ago"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make", "note": "create, produce"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very, extremely", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "to be difficult", "note": "adjective"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "에 + 는: 옛날에는 = ''in the old days'' (unlike now).", "example_in_sentence": "옛날에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. 물감을 = dye (as direct object)", "example_in_sentence": "물감을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기", "exp": "nominalizer turning verb into noun. 만들다 → 만들기 (making/to make)", "example_in_sentence": "만들기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. 만들기가 = making (as subject)", "example_in_sentence": "만들기가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending. 어렵다 → 어려웠어요 (was difficult)", "example_in_sentence": "어려웠어요"}]}, {"text": "지중해 바다에 사는 달팽이에서만 보라색을 얻을 수 있었어요.", "translation": "Purple could only be obtained from sea snails living in the Mediterranean Sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지중해", "en": "Mediterranean Sea", "note": "sea between Europe and Africa"}, {"ko": "바다", "en": "sea, ocean", "note": "large body of water"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": "reside, dwell"}, {"ko": "달팽이", "en": "snail", "note": "mollusk"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "location particle. 바다에 = in the sea", "example_in_sentence": "바다에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "present verb modifier. 살다 → 사는 (living/that live)", "example_in_sentence": "사는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "source/location particle. 달팽이에서 = from snails", "example_in_sentence": "달팽이에서만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~만", "exp": "only/just particle. restricts meaning to one thing", "example_in_sentence": "달팽이에서만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. 보라색을 = purple (as direct object)", "example_in_sentence": "보라색을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다", "exp": "ability/possibility. 얻다 → 얻을 수 있다 (can obtain)", "example_in_sentence": "얻을 수 있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending. 있다 → 있었어요 (could/was able)", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "보라색 물감 1파운드는 지금 돈으로 5만 6천 달러였어요.", "translation": "One pound of purple dye cost $56,000 in today''s money.", "vocab": [{"ko": "파운드", "en": "pound", "note": "unit of weight"}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now, present", "note": "current time"}, {"ko": "돈", "en": "money", "note": "currency"}, {"ko": "달러", "en": "dollar", "note": "US currency"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. 1파운드는 = as for one pound", "example_in_sentence": "1파운드는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "means/method particle. 돈으로 = in terms of money", "example_in_sentence": "돈으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending. copula 이다 → 였어요 (was)", "example_in_sentence": "달러였어요"}]}, {"text": "이는 정말 비싼 값이었어요.", "translation": "This was an incredibly expensive price.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정말", "en": "really, truly", "note": "adverb for emphasis"}, {"ko": "비싸다", "en": "to be expensive", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "값", "en": "price, cost", "note": "money value"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. 이는 = as for this (formal form of 이것은)", "example_in_sentence": "이는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a noun modifier: 비싸다 → 비싼 값 (an expensive price).", "example_in_sentence": "비싼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending. 이다 → 이었어요 (was)", "example_in_sentence": "값이었어요"}]}, {"text": "지금은 인공으로 보라색 물감을 만들어요.", "translation": "Now purple dye is made artificially.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금", "en": "now, present", "note": "current time"}, {"ko": "인공", "en": "artificial", "note": "man-made"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make", "note": "create, produce"}, {"ko": "물감", "en": "paint, dye", "note": "coloring material"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker with contrast. 지금은 = now (unlike before)", "example_in_sentence": "지금은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "means/method particle. 인공으로 = by artificial means", "example_in_sentence": "인공으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. 물감을 = dye (as direct object)", "example_in_sentence": "물감을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "polite present ending. 만들다 → 만들어요 (make)", "example_in_sentence": "만들어요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 값이 많이 싸졌어요.", "translation": "So the price has become much cheaper.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그래서", "en": "so, therefore", "note": "conjunction showing result"}, {"ko": "값", "en": "price, cost", "note": "money value"}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "a lot, much", "note": "adverb of quantity"}, {"ko": "싸다", "en": "to be cheap", "note": "adjective, opposite of expensive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. 값이 = price (as subject)", "example_in_sentence": "값이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다", "exp": "change of state. 싸다 → 싸지다 → 싸졌어요 (became cheap)", "example_in_sentence": "싸졌어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요", "exp": "past polite ending. 싸지다 → 싸졌어요 (became cheap)", "example_in_sentence": "싸졌어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "보라색", "en": "purple", "note": "color"}, {"ko": "국기", "en": "national flag", "note": "country''s flag"}, {"ko": "거의", "en": "almost, hardly", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to be seen, to appear", "note": "passive of 보다 (to see)"}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": "cause"}, {"ko": "물감", "en": "paint, dye", "note": "coloring material"}, {"ko": "비싸다", "en": "to be expensive", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "값", "en": "price, cost", "note": "money value"}, {"ko": "옛날", "en": "old times, 