son is the high price of purple dye."}, {"name": "~ 때문이에요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "''It is because of N''. 비싼 값 때문이에요 = it is because of the high price.", "ex_ko": "그 이유는 보라색 물감의 비싼 값 때문이에요.", "ex_en": "The reason is the high price of purple dye."}, {"name": "~에는", "level": "Starter", "exp": "에 + 는: 옛날에는 = ''in the old days'' (unlike now).", "ex_ko": "옛날에는 보라색 물감을 만들기가 매우 어려웠어요.", "ex_en": "In the past, making purple dye was extremely difficult."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Starter", "exp": "object marker. 보라색을 = purple (as direct object)", "ex_ko": "옛날에는 보라색 물감을 만들기가 매우 어려웠어요.", "ex_en": "In the past, making purple dye was extremely difficult."}, {"name": "~기", "level": "Starter", "exp": "nominalizer turning verb into noun. 만들다 → 만들기 (making/to make)", "ex_ko": "옛날에는 보라색 물감을 만들기가 매우 어려웠어요.", "ex_en": "In the past, making purple dye was extremely difficult."}, {"name": "~이/가", "level": "Starter", "exp": "subject marker. 만들기가 = making (as subject)", "ex_ko": "옛날에는 보라색 물감을 만들기가 매우 어려웠어요.", "ex_en": "In the past, making purple dye was extremely difficult."}, {"name": "~았/었/였어요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "past polite ending. 어렵다 → 어려웠어요 (was difficult)", "ex_ko": "옛날에는 보라색 물감을 만들기가 매우 어려웠어요.", "ex_en": "In the past, making purple dye was extremely difficult."}, {"name": "~는", "level": "Starter", "exp": "present verb modifier. 살다 → 사는 (living/that live)", "ex_ko": "지중해 바다에 사는 달팽이에서만 보라색을 얻을 수 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Purple could only be obtained from sea snails living in the Mediterranean Sea."}, {"name": "~만", "level": "Starter", "exp": "only/just particle. restricts meaning to one thing", "ex_ko": "지중해 바다에 사는 달팽이에서만 보라색을 얻을 수 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Purple could only be obtained from sea snails living in the Mediterranean Sea."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "ability/possibility. 얻다 → 얻을 수 있다 (can obtain)", "ex_ko": "지중해 바다에 사는 달팽이에서만 보라색을 얻을 수 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Purple could only be obtained from sea snails living in the Mediterranean Sea."}, {"name": "~(으)로", "level": "Starter", "exp": "means/method particle. 인공으로 = by artificial means", "ex_ko": "보라색 물감 1파운드는 지금 돈으로 5만 6천 달러였어요.", "ex_en": "One pound of purple dye cost $56,000 in today''s money."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp44b2pfqjgj' and md5(translation) = '31eddcecababd59cf166f06307ad35ba';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Woodpeckers are birds that peck at trees. A woodpecker''s tongue is very long.", "A woodpecker''s tongue wraps around its head. The tongue goes around the back of the head and comes out through the mouth again.", "This tongue is used when woodpeckers catch insects from tree holes. With their long tongue, they can catch insects even in deep holes.", "The woodpecker''s special tongue structure is one of nature''s amazing features. Many people are surprised when they first learn this fact."], "sentences": [{"text": "딱따구리는 나무를 쪼는 새예요.", "translation": "Woodpeckers are birds that peck at trees.", "vocab": [{"ko": "딱따구리", "en": "woodpecker", "note": "bird that pecks wood"}, {"ko": "나무", "en": "tree; wood", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쪼다", "en": "to peck; to chop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "새", "en": "bird", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "present verb modifier. Attaches to verb stems to modify nouns. 쪼다 (to peck) → 쪼는 (that pecks)", "example_in_sentence": "쪼는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. Marks direct object of action. 나무 + 를 = 나무를 (tree as object)", "example_in_sentence": "나무를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요/이에요", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 ''to be''. After a vowel use 예요: 새 → 새예요 (is a bird).", "example_in_sentence": "새예요"}]}, {"text": "딱따구리의 혀는 아주 길어요.", "translation": "A woodpecker''s tongue is very long.", "vocab": [{"ko": "혀", "en": "tongue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very; quite", "note": "adverb for emphasis"}, {"ko": "길다", "en": "to be long", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive marker. Shows ownership or relationship. 딱따구리 + 의 = 딱따구리의 (woodpecker''s)", "example_in_sentence": "딱따구리의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. Marks topic of sentence. 혀 + 는 = 혀는 (as for the tongue)", "example_in_sentence": "혀는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "present polite ending. 길다 → 길어 → 길어요 (is long, polite)", "example_in_sentence": "길어요"}]}, {"text": "딱따구리의 혀는 머리를 감싸요.", "translation": "A woodpecker''s tongue wraps around its head.", "vocab": [{"ko": "머리", "en": "head", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감싸다", "en": "to wrap; to surround", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive marker. Shows ownership or relationship. 딱따구리 + 의 = 딱따구리의 (woodpecker''s)", "example_in_sentence": "딱따구리의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. Marks topic of sentence. 혀 + 는 = 혀는 (as for the tongue)", "example_in_sentence": "혀는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. Marks direct object of action. 머리 + 를 = 머리를 (head as object)", "example_in_sentence": "머리를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "present polite ending. 감싸다 → 감싸 → 감싸요 (wraps, polite)", "example_in_sentence": "감싸요"}]}, {"text": "혀가 머리 뒤쪽을 돌아서 다시 입으로 나와요.", "translation": "The tongue goes around the back of the head and comes out through the mouth again.", "vocab": [{"ko": "혀", "en": "tongue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "머리", "en": "head", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뒤쪽", "en": "back side; rear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돌다", "en": "to turn; to go around", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. Marks subject of sentence. 혀 + 가 = 혀가 (tongue as subject)", "example_in_sentence": "혀가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. Marks direct object of action. 뒤쪽 + 을 = 뒤쪽을 (back side as object)", "example_in_sentence": "뒤쪽을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "cause or sequence connector. Shows action sequence. 돌다 → 돌아서 (go around and then)", "example_in_sentence": "돌아서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "direction or means marker. Shows direction or method. 입 + 으로 = 입으로 (through mouth)", "example_in_sentence": "입으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "present polite ending. 나오다 → 나와 → 나와요 (comes out, polite)", "example_in_sentence": "나와요"}]}, {"text": "이 혀는 딱따구리가 나무 구멍에서 벌레를 잡을 때 써요.", "translation": "This tongue is used when woodpeckers catch insects from tree holes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "구멍", "en": "hole", "note": ""}, {"ko": "벌레", "en": "insect; bug", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잡다", "en": "to catch; to grab", "note": ""}, {"ko": "때", "en": "time; when", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. Marks subject of sentence. 딱따구리 + 가 = 딱따구리가 (woodpecker as subject)", "example_in_sentence": "딱따구리가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "location marker for action. Shows where action takes place. 구멍 + 에서 = 구멍에서 (from/in hole)", "example_in_sentence": "구멍에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. Marks direct object of action. 벌레 + 를 = 벌레를 (insect as object)", "example_in_sentence": "벌레를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "exp": "when doing. Shows time of action. 잡다 → 잡을 때 (when catching)", "example_in_sentence": "잡을 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "present polite ending. 쓰다 → 써 → 써요 (uses, polite)", "example_in_sentence": "써요"}]}, {"text": "긴 혀로 깊은 구멍 안의 벌레도 잡을 수 있어요.", "translation": "With their long tongue, they can catch insects even in deep holes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "길다", "en": "to be long", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깊다", "en": "to be deep", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안", "en": "inside", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잡다", "en": "to catch; to grab", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "past verb/present adjective modifier. Modifies following noun. 길다 → 긴 (long), 깊다 → 깊은 (deep)", "example_in_sentence": "긴"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "means or instrument marker. Shows method or tool. 혀 + 로 = 혀로 (with tongue)", "example_in_sentence": "혀로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive marker. Shows ownership or relationship. 안 + 의 = 안의 (inside of)", "example_in_sentence": "안의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "also/even particle. Shows addition or emphasis. 벌레 + 도 = 벌레도 (insects too/even)", "example_in_sentence": "벌레도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "ability/possibility. Can do something. 잡다 → 잡을 수 있다 (can catch)", "example_in_sentence": "잡을 수 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "exp": "present polite informal ending", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "딱따구리의 특별한 혀 구조는 자연의 신기한 모습 중 하나예요.", "translation": "The woodpecker''s special tongue structure is one of nature''s amazing features.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구조", "en": "structure", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be mysterious", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive marker. Shows ownership or relationship. 딱따구리 + 의 = 딱따구리의 (woodpecker''s), 자연 + 의 = 자연의 (nature''s)", "example_in_sentence": "딱따구리의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "past verb/present adjective modifier. Modifies following noun. 특별하다 → 특별한 (special), 신기하다 → 신기한 (amazing)", "example_in_sentence": "특별한"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중 하나", "exp": "one of. Shows selection from a group. N 중 하나 = one of N", "example_in_sentence": "중 하나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요/이에요", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 ''to be''. After a vowel use 예요: 하나 → 하나예요 (is one).", "example_in_sentence": "하나예요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이 사실을 처음 알고 놀라워해요.", "translation": "Many people are surprised when they first learn this fact.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "fact; truth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처음", "en": "first time; beginning", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "past verb/present adjective modifier. Modifies following noun. 많다 → 많은 (many)", "example_in_sentence": "많은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. Marks subject of senten