takes place. 구멍 + 에서 = 구멍에서 (from/in hole)", "ex_ko": "이 혀는 딱따구리가 나무 구멍에서 벌레를 잡을 때 써요.", "ex_en": "This tongue is used when woodpeckers catch insects from tree holes."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "level": "Starter", "exp": "when doing. Shows time of action. 잡다 → 잡을 때 (when catching)", "ex_ko": "이 혀는 딱따구리가 나무 구멍에서 벌레를 잡을 때 써요.", "ex_en": "This tongue is used when woodpeckers catch insects from tree holes."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은", "level": "Starter", "exp": "past verb/present adjective modifier. Modifies following noun. 특별하다 → 특별한 (special), 신기하다 → 신기한 (amazing)", "ex_ko": "긴 혀로 깊은 구멍 안의 벌레도 잡을 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "With their long tongue, they can catch insects even in deep holes."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Starter", "exp": "also/even particle. Shows addition or emphasis. 벌레 + 도 = 벌레도 (insects too/even)", "ex_ko": "긴 혀로 깊은 구멍 안의 벌레도 잡을 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "With their long tongue, they can catch insects even in deep holes."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "ability/possibility. Can do something. 잡다 → 잡을 수 있다 (can catch)", "ex_ko": "긴 혀로 깊은 구멍 안의 벌레도 잡을 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "With their long tongue, they can catch insects even in deep holes."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Starter", "exp": "and connector. Links two actions in sequence. 알고 (know and)", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이 사실을 처음 알고 놀라워해요.", "ex_en": "Many people are surprised when they first learn this fact."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp44cujppo3s' and md5(translation) = 'af2d546e0406e9061f536f42679a2b30';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Facebook was first created in 2004, and it looked very different from today.", "Facebook''s first interface was very simple, using only blue and white colors.", "Today''s Facebook is complex with many features, but in 2004 it only had basic functions.", "After 20 years, Facebook has completely changed, and seeing its original form is truly fascinating."], "sentences": [{"text": "2004년에 페이스북이 처음 만들어졌어요.", "translation": "Facebook was first created in 2004.", "vocab": [{"ko": "처음", "en": "first time", "note": "adverb meaning ''for the first time''"}, {"ko": "만들어지다", "en": "to be made/created", "note": "passive form of 만들다"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 만들어지다 → 만들어졌어요 (was created)", "example_in_sentence": "만들어졌어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (time)", "exp": "Marks a point in time: 2004년 → 2004년에 (in 2004).", "example_in_sentence": "2004년에"}]}, {"text": "그때 페이스북은 지금과 많이 달랐어요.", "translation": "Back then, Facebook was very different from today.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그때", "en": "at that time/back then", "note": "time expression"}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": "present time"}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "a lot/very much", "note": "adverb of degree"}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different", "note": "descriptive verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 다르다", "exp": "''to be different from N''. 지금과 많이 달랐어요 = was very different from now.", "example_in_sentence": "지금과 많이 달랐어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 다르다 → 달랐어요 (was different)", "example_in_sentence": "달랐어요"}]}, {"text": "페이스북의 첫 번째 화면은 아주 간단했어요.", "translation": "Facebook''s first screen was very simple.", "vocab": [{"ko": "화면", "en": "screen/interface", "note": "computer/phone display"}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very/extremely", "note": "adverb intensifier"}, {"ko": "간단하다", "en": "to be simple", "note": "descriptive verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle. 페이스북의 = Facebook''s", "example_in_sentence": "페이스북의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 간단하다 → 간단했어요 (was simple)", "example_in_sentence": "간단했어요"}]}, {"text": "색깔도 파란색과 흰색만 있었어요.", "translation": "It only had blue and white colors.", "vocab": [{"ko": "색깔", "en": "color", "note": "general term for color"}, {"ko": "파란색", "en": "blue color", "note": "blue"}, {"ko": "흰색", "en": "white color", "note": "white"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist/have", "note": "existence verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also/even''. 색깔도 = even the colors", "example_in_sentence": "색깔도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "Particle connecting nouns meaning ''and''. 파란색과 흰색 = blue and white", "example_in_sentence": "파란색과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~만", "exp": "Particle meaning ''only''. 파란색과 흰색만 = only blue and white.", "example_in_sentence": "흰색만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 있다 → 있었어요 (existed/had)", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "지금 페이스북은 복잡하고 기능이 많아요.", "translation": "Today''s Facebook is complex and has many features.", "vocab": [{"ko": "복잡하다", "en": "to be complex/complicated", "note": "descriptive verb"}, {"ko": "기능", "en": "function/feature", "note": "capability or feature"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many/much", "note": "quantity adjective"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending meaning ''and''. Connects two clauses. 복잡하고 = is complex and", "example_in_sentence": "복잡하고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "Subject marker particle. 기능이 = functions (subject)", "example_in_sentence": "기능이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 많다 → 많아요 (are many)", "example_in_sentence": "많아요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 2004년에는 기본적인 기능만 있었어요.", "translation": "But in 2004, it only had basic functions.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but/however", "note": "conjunction showing contrast"}, {"ko": "기본적", "en": "basic/fundamental", "note": "adjective modifier"}, {"ko": "기능", "en": "function/feature", "note": "capability or feature"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "Time/location particle 에 + topic particle 는. 2004년에는 = in 2004 (topic)", "example_in_sentence": "2004년에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~만", "exp": "Particle meaning ''only''. 기능만 = only functions", "example_in_sentence": "기능만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 있다 → 있었어요 (existed/had)", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "20년이 지난 지금 페이스북은 완전히 바뀌었어요.", "translation": "Now, 20 years later, Facebook has completely changed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "년", "en": "year", "note": "counter for years"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass/go by", "note": "time passing"}, {"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely/totally", "note": "adverb of degree"}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change/be changed", "note": "intransitive verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "Subject marker particle. 20년이 = 20 years (subject)", "example_in_sentence": "20년이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "Past modifier ending. 지나다 → 지난 (that passed). Modifies 지금", "example_in_sentence": "지난"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 바뀌다 → 바뀌었어요 (changed)", "example_in_sentence": "바뀌었어요"}]}, {"text": "첫 번째 모습을 보면 정말 신기해요.", "translation": "Looking at its original form is really fascinating.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance/form", "note": "how something looks"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see/look at", "note": "basic verb"}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really/truly", "note": "adverb intensifier"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be fascinating/amazing", "note": "descriptive verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object marker particle. 모습을 = appearance (object)", "example_in_sentence": "모습을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Conditional ending meaning ''if/when''. 보다 → 보면 (if you look/when looking)", "example_in_sentence": "보면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 신기하다 → 신기해요 (is fascinating)", "example_in_sentence": "신기해요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "처음", "en": "first time", "note": "adverb meaning ''for the first time''"}, {"ko": "만들어지다", "en": "to be made/created", "note": "passive form of 만들다"}, {"ko": "그때", "en": "at that time/back then", "note": "time expression"}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": "present time"}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "a lot/very much", "note": "adverb of degree"}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different", "note": "descriptive verb"}, {"ko": "화면", "en": "screen/interface", "note": "computer/phone display"}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very/extremely", "note": "adverb intensifier"}, {"ko": "간단하다", "en": "to be simple", "note": "descriptive verb"}, {"ko": "색깔", "en": "color", "note": "general term for color"}, {"ko": "파란색", "en": "blue color", "note": "blue"}, {"ko": "흰색", "en": "white color", "note": "white"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist/have", "note": "existence verb"}, {"ko": "복잡하다", "en": "to be complex/complicated", "note": "descriptive verb"}, {"ko": "기능", "en": "function/feature", "note": "capability or feature"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many/much", "note": "quantity adjective"}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but/however", "note": "conjunction showing contrast"}, {"ko": "기본적", "en": "basic/fundamental", "note": "adjective modifier"}, {"ko": "년", "en": "year", "note": "counter for years"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass/go by", "note": "time passing"}, {"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely/totally", "note": "adverb of degree"}, {"ko": "바뀌다", "en": "to change/be changed", "note": "intransitive verb"}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance/form", "note": "how something looks"}, {"ko": "보다", "