: "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 신기하다 → 신기해요 (is fascinating)", "ex_ko": "지금 페이스북은 복잡하고 기능이 많아요.", "ex_en": "Today''s Facebook is complex and has many features."}, {"name": "~에는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Time/location particle 에 + topic particle 는. 2004년에는 = in 2004 (topic)", "ex_ko": "하지만 2004년에는 기본적인 기능만 있었어요.", "ex_en": "But in 2004, it only had basic functions."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past modifier ending. 지나다 → 지난 (that passed). Modifies 지금", "ex_ko": "20년이 지난 지금 페이스북은 완전히 바뀌었어요.", "ex_en": "Now, 20 years later, Facebook has completely changed."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Object marker particle. 모습을 = appearance (object)", "ex_ko": "첫 번째 모습을 보면 정말 신기해요.", "ex_en": "Looking at its original form is really fascinating."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Conditional ending meaning ''if/when''. 보다 → 보면 (if you look/when looking)", "ex_ko": "첫 번째 모습을 보면 정말 신기해요.", "ex_en": "Looking at its original form is really fascinating."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp44dxafcoae' and md5(translation) = '7d3a30887420f7abbef750a892ef50b6';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A small squid living in the sea uses a special technique. This squid''s name is the bobtail squid. On nights when there is moonlight, the squid creates a shadow on the sea floor. Because of this shadow, dangerous fish can easily find the squid. The bobtail squid produces light from its own body. This light is called bioluminescence. The squid uses this light to eliminate or reduce its shadow. In this way, the squid protects itself from dangerous fish. Nature really has amazing methods.", "Korean teacher shortage crisis worsens, disrupting school classes", "What is an ''anxiety bag''? A popular trend", "The US and China resume talks over trade issues", "\"Talking pig\" becomes an SNS star", "''Nothing maxing'' trend spreads—doing absolutely nothing"], "sentences": [{"text": "바다에 사는 작은 오징어가 특별한 기술을 사용해요.", "translation": "Small squid living in the sea use special techniques.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바다", "en": "sea"}, {"ko": "오징어", "en": "squid"}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technique"}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "Present modifier for verbs. 살다 (to live) drops ㄹ before -는: 바다에 사는 오징어 = squid that live in the sea.", "example_in_sentence": "바다에 사는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (polite present)", "exp": "Polite present ending. 하다 verbs become 해요: 사용하다 → 사용해요 (use).", "example_in_sentence": "사용해요"}]}, {"text": "이 오징어의 이름은 보브테일 오징어예요.", "translation": "This squid''s name is bobtail squid.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이름", "en": "name"}, {"ko": "보브테일 오징어", "en": "bobtail squid"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive particle)", "exp": "Marks possession or attribution between nouns. 오징어 (squid) + 의 + 이름 (name).", "example_in_sentence": "오징어의 이름은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요 (polite copula)", "exp": "Polite form of ~이다 (to be) for identification. Used after vowels or no final consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "예요"}]}, {"text": "달빛이 있는 밤에 오징어는 바다 바닥에 그림자를 만들어요.", "translation": "On nights when there is moonlight, squid create shadows on the sea floor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "달빛", "en": "moonlight"}, {"ko": "밤", "en": "night"}, {"ko": "바닥", "en": "bottom/floor"}, {"ko": "그림자", "en": "shadow"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (relative clause modifier)", "exp": "Modifies the following noun. 있다 (to exist) → 있는 (existing).", "example_in_sentence": "달빛이 있는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (time / place)", "exp": "Marks time or place: 밤 → 밤에 (at night), 바닥 → 바닥에 (on the floor).", "example_in_sentence": "밤에"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "그림자를 만들다 (to create/cast a shadow)", "exp": "Verb phrase expressing the action of producing or forming a shadow.", "example_in_sentence": "그림자를 만들어요"}]}, {"text": "이 그림자 때문에 위험한 물고기들이 오징어를 쉽게 찾을 수 있어요.", "translation": "Because of this shadow, dangerous fish can easily find squid.", "vocab": [{"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous"}, {"ko": "물고기", "en": "fish"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~때문에 (because of/due to)", "exp": "Expresses cause or reason. Noun + 때문에.", "example_in_sentence": "이 그림자 때문에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Shows ability or possibility, ''can''. 찾다 → 찾을 수 있어요 (can find).", "example_in_sentence": "찾을 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "보브테일 오징어는 자신의 몸에서 빛을 만들어요.", "translation": "Bobtail squid create light from their own body.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself/self"}, {"ko": "몸", "en": "body"}, {"ko": "빛", "en": "light"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive particle)", "exp": "Marks possession between nouns. 자신 (self) + 의 + 몸 (body).", "example_in_sentence": "자신의 몸에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (source/origin particle)", "exp": "Marks the source or origin point. 몸 (body) + 에서.", "example_in_sentence": "몸에서"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "빛을 만들다 (to produce/emit light)", "exp": "Verb phrase expressing the action of generating or emitting light.", "example_in_sentence": "빛을 만들어요"}]}, {"text": "이 빛을 생물발광이라고 해요.", "translation": "This light is called bioluminescence.", "vocab": [{"ko": "생물발광", "en": "bioluminescence"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~라고 하다 (to be called/to say)", "exp": "Expresses naming or reporting. Noun + (이)라고 하다. 생물발광 + 이라고 해요.", "example_in_sentence": "생물발광이라고 해요"}]}, {"text": "오징어는 이 빛으로 그림자를 없애거나 작게 만들어요.", "translation": "With this light, squid remove their shadows or make them smaller.", "vocab": [{"ko": "없애다", "en": "to eliminate/remove"}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~으로 (means/tool particle)", "exp": "Marks the means or instrument used. 빛 (light) + 으로.", "example_in_sentence": "이 빛으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~거나 (or)", "exp": "Connects two choices, ''or'': 없애다 → 없애거나 작게 만들어요 (remove it or make it small).", "example_in_sentence": "없애거나"}]}, {"text": "이런 방법으로 오징어는 위험한 물고기들로부터 자신을 보호해요.", "translation": "In this way, squid protect themselves from dangerous fish.", "vocab": [{"ko": "방법", "en": "method/way"}, {"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~으로 (means/method particle)", "exp": "Marks the means or manner. 방법 (method) + 으로.", "example_in_sentence": "이런 방법으로"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~로부터 (from/away from)", "exp": "Marks source of separation or protection. 물고기들 + 로부터.", "example_in_sentence": "물고기들로부터"}]}, {"text": "자연은 정말 신기한 방법들을 가지고 있어요.", "translation": "Nature truly has amazing methods.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자연", "en": "nature"}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really/truly"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing/curious"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (continuous aspect)", "exp": "Indicates an ongoing or maintained state. 가지다 (to have) → 가지고 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "가지고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "바다", "en": "sea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오징어", "en": "squid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보브테일 오징어", "en": "bobtail squid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달빛", "en": "moonlight", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밤", "en": "night", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바닥", "en": "bottom/floor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그림자", "en": "shadow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "to be dangerous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물고기", "en": "fish", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself/self", "note": ""}, {"ko": "몸", "en": "body", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빛", "en": "light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생물발광", "en": "bioluminescence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "없애다", "en": "to eliminate/remove", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method/way", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really/truly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing/curious", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보브테일", "en": "bobtail", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 (relative clause modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present modifier for verbs. 살다 (to live) drops ㄹ before -는: 바다에 사는 오징어 = squid that live in the sea.", "ex_ko": "바다에 사는 작은 오징어가 특별한 기술을 사용해요.", "ex_en": "Small squid living in the sea use special techniques."}, {"name": "~아/어요 (polite present)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Polite present ending. 하다 verbs become 해요: 사용하다 → 사용해요 (use).", "ex_ko": "바다에 사는 작은 오징어가 특별한 기술을 사용해요.", "ex_en": "Small squid living in the sea use special techniques."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks possession or attribution between nouns. 오징어 (squid) + 의 + 이름 (name).", "ex_ko": "이 오징어의 이름은 보브테일 오징어예요.", "ex_en": "This squid''s name is bobtail squid."}, {"name": "~예요 (polite copula)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Polite form of ~이다 (to be) for identification. Used after vowels or no final consonant.", "ex_ko": "이 오징어의 이름은 보브테일 오징어예요.", "ex_en": "This squid''s name is bobtail squid."}, {"name": "~에서 (source/origin particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks time or place: 밤 → 밤에 (at night), 바닥 → 바닥에 (on the floor).", "ex_ko": "달빛이 있는 밤에 오징어는 바다 바닥에 그림자를 만들어요.", "ex_en": "On nights when there is moonlight, squid create shadows on the sea floor."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows ability or possibility, ''can''. 찾다 → 찾을 수 있어요 (can find).", "ex_ko": "이 그림자 때문에 위험한 물고기들이 오징어를 쉽게 찾을 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Because of this shadow, dangerous fish can easily find squid."}, {"name": "~으로 (means/method particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the means or instrument used. 빛 (light) + 으로.", "ex_ko": "오징어는 이 빛으로 그림자를 없애거나 작게 만들어요.", "ex_en": "With this light, squid remove their shadows or make them smaller."}, {"name": "~거나 (or)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connects two choices, ''or'': 없애다 → 없애거나 작게 만들어요 (remove it or make it small).", "ex_ko": "오징어는 이 빛으로 그림자를 없애거나 작게 만들어요.", "ex_en": "With this light, squid remove their shadows or make them smaller."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (continuous aspect)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Indicates an ongoing or maintained state. 가지다 (to have) → 가지고 있어요.", "ex_ko": "자연은 정말 신기한 방법들을 가지고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Nature truly has amazing methods."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp44expbyfq1' and md5(translation) = '4db6e0eeafa6d180195bf7ddcc901773';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 1841, a free black man named Solomon Northup traveled to Washington DC, where he was kidnapped.", "The kidnappers took him to Louisiana and sold him into slavery, though Northup was a free man with no way to prove it.", "After 12 years, Northup was finally able to prove his freedom and escaped from slavery.", "His kidnapper was brought to trial, but Washington DC law prohibited black people from testifying against white people, resulting in an acquittal."], "sentences": [{"text": "1841년 솔로몬 노섭이라는 자유 흑인 남성이 워싱턴DC로 여행을 떠났어요.", "translation": "In 1841, a free black man named Solomon Northup traveled to Washington DC.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자유", "en": "freedom; free", "note": "free (adjective when used as modifier)"}, {"ko": "흑인", "en": "black person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남성", "en": "man, male", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여행", "en": "travel, trip", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는", "exp": "adnominal form meaning ''called/named''. Used to identify or introduce someone/something by name. 솔로몬 노섭이라는 = ''(a man) called Solomon Northup''", "example_in_sentence": "솔로몬 노섭이라는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "particle indicating direction or destination. 워싱턴DC로 = ''to Washington DC''", "example_in_sentence": "워싱턴DC로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending: 떠나다 (to leave) → 떠났어요 (left).", "example_in_sentence": "떠났어요"}]}, {"text": "그런데 그곳에서 납치를 당했습니다.", "translation": "However, he was kidnapped there.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그런데", "en": "however, but", "note": "conjunction showing contrast"}, {"ko": "그곳", "en": "that place, there", "note": ""}, {"ko": "납치", "en": "kidnapping", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당하다", "en": "to suffer, to be subjected to", "note": "passive meaning"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 당하다", "exp": "passive construction meaning ''to suffer/experience something (usually negative)''. 납치를 당하다 = ''to be kidnapped''", "example_in_sentence": "납치를 당했습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였습니다", "exp": "Past formal ending: 당하다 → 당했습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "당했습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "at/in (location of action) or from (source)", "example_in_sentence": "그곳에서"}]}, {"text": "납치범들은 그를 루이지애나주로 데려가서 노예로 팔았어요.", "translation": "The kidnappers took him to Louisiana and sold him as a slave.", "vocab": [{"ko": "납치범", "en": "kidnapper", "note": "범 = criminal"}, {"ko": "데려가다", "en": "to take (someone somewhere)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "노예", "en": "slave", "note": ""}, {"ko": "팔다", "en": "to sell", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "connective ending showing sequence or cause. 데려가다 → 데려가 + 아서 → 데려가서 (took and then...)", "example_in_sentence": "데려가서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "particle indicating means, method, or role. 노예로 = ''as a slave''", "example_in_sentence": "노예로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending: 팔다 (to sell) → 팔았어요 (sold).", "example_in_sentence": "팔았어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (direction)", "exp": "Marks the destination: 루이지애나주 → 루이지애나주로 (to Louisiana).", "example_in_sentence": "루이지애나주로"}]}, {"text": "노섭은 자유인이었지만 증명할 방법이 없었습니다.", "translation": "Northup was a free man, but had no way to prove it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자유인", "en": "free person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "증명하다", "en": "to prove, to verify", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method, way", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만", "exp": "connective ending meaning ''but/although''. Shows contrast between clauses.", "example_in_sentence": "이었지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ", "exp": "adnominal ending for future/hypothetical. 증명하다 → 증명할 (method to prove)", "example_in_sentence": "증명할"}]}, {"text": "12년이 지나서야 노섭은 자신이 자유인이라는 것을 증명할 수 있었어요.", "translation": "Only after 12 years had passed was Northup able to prove that he was a free man.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass (time)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself", "note": ""}, {"ko": "증명하다", "en": "to prove", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서야", "exp": "''only after ~''. 지나다 → 지나서야 (only after (12 years) had passed).", "example_in_sentence": "지나서야"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는 것", "exp": "''the fact that ...''. 자유인이다 → 자유인이라는 것 (the fact that he is a free man).", "example_in_sentence": "자유인이라는 것을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "ability/possibility expression. 증명하다 → 증명할 수 있다 (can prove)", "example_in_sentence": "증명할 수 있었어요"}]}, {"text": "그는 마침내 노예 생활에서 벗어났습니다.", "translation": "He finally escaped from slave life.", "vocab": [{"ko": "마침내", "en": "finally, at last", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생활", "en": "life, living", "note": ""}, {"ko": "벗어나다", "en": "to escape from, to get out of", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "at/in (location of action) or from (source)", "example_in_sentence": "생활에서"}]}, {"text": "노섭을 납치한 범인이 법정에 서게 되었어요.", "translation": "The criminal who kidnapped Northup came to stand trial in court.", "vocab": [{"ko": "납치하다", "en": "to kidnap", "note": ""}, {"ko": "범인", "en": "criminal, culprit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "법정", "en": "courtroom, court", "note": ""}, {"ko": "서다", "en": "to stand", "note": "here means ''to stand trial''"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "past adnominal ending. 납치하다 → 납치한 (who kidnapped)", "example_in_sentence": "납치한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "''to end up / come to V'', a change brought about by circumstances. 서다 → 서게 되었어요 (ended up standing (trial)).", "example_in_sentence": "서게 되었어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 당시 워싱턴DC 법에 따르면 흑인은 백인에 대해 증언할 수 없었습니다.", "translation": "However, according to Washington DC law at the time, black people could not testify against white people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "법", "en": "law", "note": ""}, {"ko": "백인", "en": "white person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "증언하다", "en": "to testify", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에 따르면", "exp": "according to, based on. Used to cite sources or standards.", "example_in_sentence": "법에 따르면"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에 대해", "exp": "about, regarding, against. 백인에 대해 = ''against white people''", "example_in_sentence": "백인에 대해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다", "exp": "inability/impossibility. 증언하다 → 증언할 수 없다 (cannot testify)", "example_in_sentence": "증언할 수 없었습니다"}]}, {"text": "결국 범인은 무죄 판결을 받았어요.", "translation": "In the end, the criminal received a not guilty verdict.", "vocab": [{"ko": "결국", "en": "in the end, finally", "note": ""}, {"ko": "범인", "en": "criminal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무죄", "en": "not guilty, innocent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "판결", "en": "verdict, judgment", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending: 받다 → 받았어요 (received).", "example_in_sentence": "받았어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "자유", "en": "freedom; free", "note": "free (adjective when used as modifier)"}, {"ko": "흑인", "en": "black person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남성", "en": "man, male", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여행", "en": "travel, trip", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그런데", "en": "however, but", "note": "conjunction showing contrast"}, {"ko": "그곳", "en": "that place, there", "note": ""}, {"ko": "납치", "en": "kidnapping", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당하다", "en": "to suffer, to be subjected to", "note": "passive meaning"}, {"ko": "납치범", "en": "kidnapper", "note": "범 = criminal"}, {"ko": "데려가다", "en": "to take (someone somewhere)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "노예", "en": "slave", "note": ""}, {"ko": "팔다", "en": "to sell", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자유인", "en": "free person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "증명하다", "en": "to prove, to verify", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method, way", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass (time)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마침내", "en": "finally, at last", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생활", "en": "life, living", "note": ""}, {"ko": "벗어나다", "en": "to escape from, to get out of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "납치하다", "en": "to kidnap", "note": ""}, {"ko": "범인", "en": "criminal, culprit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "법정", "en": "courtroom, court", "note": ""}, {"ko": "서다", "en": "to stand", "note": "here means ''to stand trial''"}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "법", "en": "law", "note": ""}, {"ko": "백인", "en": "white person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "증언하다", "en": "to testify", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결국", "en": "in the end, finally", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무죄", "en": "not guilty, innocent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "판결", "en": "verdict, judgment", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(이)라는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "adnominal form meaning ''called/named''. Used to identify or introduce someone/something by name. 솔로몬 노섭이라는 = ''(a man) called Solomon Northup''", "ex_ko": "1841년 솔로몬 노섭이라는 자유 흑인 남성이 워싱턴DC로 여행을 떠났어요.", "ex_en": "In 1841, a free black man named Solomon Northup traveled to Washington DC."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (direction)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "particle indicating direction or destination. 워싱턴DC로 = ''to Washington DC''", "ex_ko": "1841년 솔로몬 노섭이라는 자유 흑인 남성이 워싱턴DC로 여행을 떠났어요.", "ex_en": "In 1841, a free black man named Solomon Northup traveled to Washington DC."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past polite ending: 떠나다 (to leave) → 떠났어요 (left).", "ex_ko": "1841년 솔로몬 노섭이라는 자유 흑인 남성이 워싱턴DC로 여행을 떠났어요.", "ex_en": "In 1841, a free black man named Solomon Northup traveled to Washington DC."}, {"name": "~았/었/였습니다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past formal ending: 당하다 → 당했습니다.", "ex_ko": "그런데 그곳에서 납치를 당했습니다.", "ex_en": "However, he was kidnapped there."}, {"name": "~에서 (location/source)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "at/in (location of action) or from (source)", "ex_ko": "그런데 그곳에서 납치를 당했습니다.", "ex_en": "However, he was kidnapped there."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "connective ending showing sequence or cause. 데려가다 → 데려가 + 아서 → 데려가서 (took and then...)", "ex_ko": "납치범들은 그를 루이지애나주로 데려가서 노예로 팔았어요.", "ex_en": "The kidnappers took him to Louisiana and sold him as a slave."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "connective ending meaning ''but/although''. Shows contrast between clauses.", "ex_ko": "노섭은 자유인이었지만 증명할 방법이 없었습니다.", "ex_en": "Northup was a free man, but had no way to prove it."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "adnominal ending for future/hypothetical. 증명하다 → 증명할 (method to prove)", "ex_ko": "노섭은 자유인이었지만 증명할 방법이 없었습니다.", "ex_en": "Northup was a free man, but had no way to prove it."}, {"name": "~아/어서야", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''only after ~''. 지나다 → 지나서야 (only after (12 years) had passed).", "ex_ko": "12년이 지나서야 노섭은 자신이 자유인이라는 것을 증명할 수 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Only after 12 years had passed was Northup able to prove that he was a free man."}, {"name": "~(이)라는 것", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''the fact that ...''. 자유인이다 → 자유인이라는 것 (the fact that he is a free man).", "ex_ko": "12년이 지나서야 노섭은 자신이 자유인이라는 것을 증명할 수 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Only after 12 years had passed was Northup able to prove that he was a free man."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "ability/possibility expression. 증명하다 → 증명할 수 있다 (can prove)", "ex_ko": "12년이 지나서야 노섭은 자신이 자유인이라는 것을 증명할 수 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Only after 12 years had passed was Northup able to prove that he was a free man."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "past adnominal ending. 납치하다 → 납치한 (who kidnapped)", "ex_ko": "노섭을 납치한 범인이 법정에 서게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "The criminal who kidnapped Northup came to stand trial in court."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''to end up / come to V'', a change brought about by circumstances. 서다 → 서게 되었어요 (ended up standing (trial)).", "ex_ko": "노섭을 납치한 범인이 법정에 서게 되었어요.", "ex_en": "The criminal who kidnapped Northup came to stand trial in court."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "inability/impossibility. 증언하다 → 증언할 수 없다 (cannot testify)", "ex_ko": "하지만 당시 워싱턴DC 법에 따르면 흑인은 백인에 대해 증언할 수 없었습니다.", "ex_en": "However, according to Washington DC law at the time, black people could not testify against white people."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp44g33prd3v' and md5(translation) = '5affdfe91e18ad3faecfcc7be7a73ac6';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["The youngest woman executed under UK law in the 20th century was Irma Grese. She was 22 years old at the time of her execution.", "Grese was called ''the hyena of Auschwitz''. This nickname reflected her cruelty.", "She wanted to become a concentration camp guard before turning 18. However, her initial application was rejected.", "The authorities told her to wait until she came of age and then return. Eventually, she later became a concentration camp guard."], "sentences": [{"text": "20세기 영국 법에 따라 사형당한 가장 젊은 여성은 이르마 그레세였어요.", "translation": "The youngest woman executed under UK law in the 20th century was Irma Grese.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세기", "en": "century", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사형당하다", "en": "to be executed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "젊다", "en": "to be young", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 따라(서)", "exp": "according to / in accordance with. 법에 따라 = according to the law.", "example_in_sentence": "법에 따라"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이었어요/였어요 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past polite form of 이다 ''to be''. After a vowel it shortens to 였어요: 그레세 → 그레세였어요 (was Grese).", "example_in_sentence": "그레세였어요"}]}, {"text": "그녀는 사형 당시 22세였습니다.", "translation": "She was 22 years old at the time of her execution.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사형", "en": "execution, death penalty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time, then", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그레세는 ''아우슈비츠의 하이에나''라고 불렸어요.", "translation": "Grese was called ''the hyena of Auschwitz''.", "vocab": [{"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call, to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하이에나", "en": "hyena", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고", "exp": "quotative particle for names/titles. Used when quoting what someone/something is called.", "example_in_sentence": "''아우슈비츠의 하이에나''라고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "불리다 (passive of 부르다)", "exp": "부르다 (to call) → 불리다 (to be called) → 불렸어요 (was called).", "example_in_sentence": "불렸어요"}]}, {"text": "이 별명은 그녀의 잔혹함을 나타내는 표현이었습니다.", "translation": "This nickname reflected her cruelty.", "vocab": [{"ko": "별명", "en": "nickname", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잔혹함", "en": "cruelty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나타내다", "en": "to show, to express, to represent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "표현", "en": "expression", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "present tense verb modifier. 나타내다 → 나타내는 표현 (expression that shows).", "example_in_sentence": "나타내는"}]}, {"text": "그녀는 18세가 되기 전에 집중수용소 간수가 되고 싶어 했어요.", "translation": "She wanted to become a concentration camp guard before turning 18.", "vocab": [{"ko": "집중수용소", "en": "concentration camp", "note": ""}, {"ko": "간수", "en": "guard, prison guard", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 전에", "exp": "before V-ing. 되다 → 되기 전에 (before becoming).", "example_in_sentence": "되기 전에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 싶어 하다", "exp": "want to (third person). 되다 → 되고 싶어 했어요 (wanted to become).", "example_in_sentence": "되고 싶어 했어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 처음에는 지원이 거부당했습니다.", "translation": "However, her initial application was rejected.", "vocab": [{"ko": "처음", "en": "first, beginning", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지원", "en": "application, support", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거부당하다", "en": "to be rejected, to be refused", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "topic marker with time/location. 처음에는 = as for the beginning/initially.", "example_in_sentence": "처음에는"}]}, {"text": "당시 당국은 그녀에게 성년이 될 때까지 기다렸다가 다시 오라고 말했어요.", "translation": "At the time, the authorities told her to wait until she came of age and then come back.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당국", "en": "authorities", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성년", "en": "adulthood, coming of age", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기다리다", "en": "to wait", "note": ""}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to say, to tell", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 때까지", "exp": "until (time when). 될 때까지 = until (she) becomes.", "example_in_sentence": "될 때까지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었다가", "exp": "after doing, then. 기다리다 → 기다렸다가 (after waiting).", "example_in_sentence": "기다렸다가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)라고 하다", "exp": "indirect imperative. Reports commands or requests. 오다 → 오라고 말했어요 (told to come).", "example_in_sentence": "오라고 말했어요"}]}, {"text": "결국 그녀는 나중에 집중수용소 간수가 되었습니다.", "translation": "Eventually, she later became a concentration camp guard.", "vocab": [{"ko": "결국", "en": "eventually, in the end", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나중에", "en": "later", "note": ""}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "세기", "en": "century", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사형당하다", "en": "to be executed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "젊다", "en": "to be young", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사형", "en": "execution, death penalty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time, then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call, to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하이에나", "en": "hyena", "note": ""}, {"ko": "별명", "en": "nickname", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잔혹함", "en": "cruelty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나타내다", "en": "to show, to express, to represent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "표현", "en": "expression", "note": ""}, {"ko": "집중수용소", "en": "concentration camp", "note": ""}, {"ko": "간수", "en": "guard, prison guard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처음", "en": "first, beginning", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지원", "en": "application, support", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거부당하다", "en": "to be rejected, to be refused", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당국", "en": "authorities", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성년", "en": "adulthood, coming of age", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기다리다", "en": "to wait", "note": ""}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to say, to tell", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결국", "en": "eventually, in the end", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나중에", "en": "later", "note": ""}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~에 따라(서)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "according to / in accordance with. 법에 따라 = according to the law.", "ex_ko": "20세기 영국 법에 따라 사형당한 가장 젊은 여성은 이르마 그레세였어요.", "ex_en": "The youngest woman executed under UK law in the 20th century was Irma Grese."}, {"name": "~이었어요/였어요 (past of 이다)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past polite form of 이다 ''to be''. After a vowel it shortens to 였어요: 그레세 → 그레세였어요 (was Grese).", "ex_ko": "20세기 영국 법에 따라 사형당한 가장 젊은 여성은 이르마 그레세였어요.", "ex_en": "The youngest woman executed under UK law in the 20th century was Irma Grese."}, {"name": "~(이)라고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "quotative particle for names/titles. Used when quoting what someone/something is called.", "ex_ko": "그레세는 ''아우슈비츠의 하이에나''라고 불렸어요.", "ex_en": "Grese was called ''the hyena of Auschwitz''."}, {"name": "불리다 (passive of 부르다)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "부르다 (to call) → 불리다 (to be called) → 불렸어요 (was called).", "ex_ko": "그레세는 ''아우슈비츠의 하이에나''라고 불렸어요.", "ex_en": "Grese was called ''the hyena of Auschwitz''."}, {"name": "~는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "present tense verb modifier. 나타내다 → 나타내는 표현 (expression that shows).", "ex_ko": "이 별명은 그녀의 잔혹함을 나타내는 표현이었습니다.", "ex_en": "This nickname reflected her cruelty."}, {"name": "~기 전에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "before V-ing. 되다 → 되기 전에 (before becoming).", "ex_ko": "그녀는 18세가 되기 전에 집중수용소 간수가 되고 싶어 했어요.", "ex_en": "She wanted to become a concentration camp guard before turning 18."}, {"name": "~고 싶어 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "want to (third person). 되다 → 되고 싶어 했어요 (wanted to become).", "ex_ko": "그녀는 18세가 되기 전에 집중수용소 간수가 되고 싶어 했어요.", "ex_en": "She wanted to become a concentration camp guard before turning 18."}, {"name": "~에는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "topic marker with time/location. 처음에는 = as for the beginning/initially.", "ex_ko": "하지만 처음에는 지원이 거부당했습니다.", "ex_en": "However, her initial application was rejected."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 때까지", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "until (time when). 될 때까지 = until (she) becomes.", "ex_ko": "당시 당국은 그녀에게 성년이 될 때까지 기다렸다가 다시 오라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "At the time, the authorities told her to wait until she came of age and then come back."}, {"name": "~았/었다가", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "after doing, then. 기다리다 → 기다렸다가 (after waiting).", "ex_ko": "당시 당국은 그녀에게 성년이 될 때까지 기다렸다가 다시 오라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "At the time, the authorities told her to wait until she came of age and then come back."}, {"name": "~(으)라고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "indirect imperative. Reports commands or requests. 오다 → 오라고 말했어요 (told to come).", "ex_ko": "당시 당국은 그녀에게 성년이 될 때까지 기다렸다가 다시 오라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "At the time, the authorities told her to wait until she came of age and then come back."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp44gy4xnhpj' and md5(translation) = '66295ad3daf67aa7a01d4dfbaed73ced';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["American firefighter Donald Herbert showed an amazing recovery. He lost consciousness in an accident during firefighting work.", "After the accident, he fell into a deep coma for one year. Even after waking up, he couldn''t recognize family or friends.", "After that, a minimally conscious state continued for over nine years. Even doctors found it difficult to expect a complete recovery.", "But a miracle happened. After 10 years, he completely regained consciousness. His first question after waking up was about his wife."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국의 소방관 도널드 허버트가 놀라운 회복을 보였습니다.", "translation": "American firefighter Donald Herbert showed an amazing recovery.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소방관", "en": "firefighter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "amazing, surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "회복", "en": "recovery", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "show, display", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "formal past tense ending. 보이다 (show) → 보였다 → 보였습니다", "example_in_sentence": "보였습니다"}]}, {"text": "그는 소방 작업 중 사고를 당해 의식을 잃었어요.", "translation": "He lost consciousness in an accident during firefighting work.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소방", "en": "firefighting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작업", "en": "work, operation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사고", "en": "accident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당하다", "en": "suffer, be subjected to", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~중", "exp": "in the middle of, during. 작업 (work) + 중 = during work", "example_in_sentence": "소방 작업 중"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "cause/sequence connector. 당하다 → 당해서 → 당해 (contracted). Shows the accident happened and as a result he lost consciousness", "example_in_sentence": "당해"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "의식을 잃다", "exp": "idiomatic expression meaning ''to lose consciousness'' or ''to faint''", "example_in_sentence": "의식을 잃었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending: 잃다 → 잃었어요 (lost).", "example_in_sentence": "잃었어요"}]}, {"text": "사고 후 그는 1년간 깊은 혼수상태에 빠졌습니다.", "translation": "After the accident, he fell into a deep coma for one year.", "vocab": [{"ko": "후", "en": "after", "note": ""}, {"ko": "년간", "en": "for ... years", "note": "duration marker"}, {"ko": "깊다", "en": "deep", "note": ""}, {"ko": "혼수상태", "en": "coma", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 빠지다", "exp": "fall into a state. Used with abstract states like 혼수상태 (coma), 절망 (despair)", "example_in_sentence": "혼수상태에 빠졌습니다"}]}, {"text": "깨어난 후에도 가족이나 친구들을 알아보지 못했어요.", "translation": "Even after waking up, he couldn''t recognize family or friends.", "vocab": [{"ko": "깨어나다", "en": "wake up, come to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": ""}, {"ko": "친구", "en": "friend", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알아보다", "en": "recognize", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 후에", "exp": "after V-ing. 깨어나다 → 깨어난 + 후에 = after waking up", "example_in_sentence": "깨어난 후에도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에도", "exp": "even (at/to). Shows contrast - even after waking up, still couldn''t recognize", "example_in_sentence": "후에도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)나", "exp": "or, choice between options. 가족이나 친구들 = family or friends", "example_in_sentence": "가족이나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다", "exp": "cannot, inability. 알아보다 → 알아보지 못하다 = cannot recognize", "example_in_sentence": "알아보지 못했어요"}]}, {"text": "그 후 9년이 넘는 시간 동안 최소의식상태가 계속되었습니다.", "translation": "After that, a minimally conscious state continued for over nine years.", "vocab": [{"ko": "넘다", "en": "exceed, go over", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during, for (duration)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "최소의식상태", "en": "minimally conscious state", "note": "medical term"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "present modifier for verbs. 넘다 → 넘는 (time that exceeds)", "example_in_sentence": "넘는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 동안", "exp": "''for / during (a period)''. 9년이 넘는 시간 동안 = for more than nine years.", "example_in_sentence": "시간 동안"}]}, {"text": "의사들도 완전한 회복을 기대하기 어려웠어요.", "translation": "Even doctors found it difficult to expect a complete recovery.", "vocab": [{"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완전하다", "en": "complete, perfect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기대하다", "en": "expect, hope for", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "difficult, hard", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 어렵다", "exp": "difficult to V. Pattern: V-기 + 어렵다 = hard to do V", "example_in_sentence": "기대하기 어려웠어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (even)", "exp": "''even / also''. 의사들도 = even the doctors.", "example_in_sentence": "의사들도"}]}, {"text": "하지만 기적이 일어났습니다.", "translation": "But a miracle happened.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기적", "en": "miracle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "happen, occur", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "10년 만에 그가 완전히 의식을 되찾았어요.", "translation": "After 10 years, he completely regained consciousness.", "vocab": [{"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "되찾다", "en": "regain, get back", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~만에", "exp": "after a duration of time. Shows something happens after a long period. 10년 만에 = after 10 years", "example_in_sentence": "10년 만에"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "의식을 되찾다", "exp": "idiomatic expression meaning ''to regain consciousness''", "example_in_sentence": "의식을 되찾았어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending: 되찾다 → 되찾았어요 (regained).", "example_in_sentence": "되찾았어요"}]}, {"text": "깨어난 후 그의 첫 번째 질문은 아내에 대한 것이었습니다.", "translation": "His first question after waking up was about his wife.", "vocab": [{"ko": "첫 번째", "en": "first", "note": "ordinal number"}, {"ko": "질문", "en": "question", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 대한", "exp": "about, regarding. Adnominal form. 아내에 대한 것 = (thing) about his wife", "example_in_sentence": "아내에 대한"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "소방관", "en": "firefighter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "amazing, surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "회복", "en": "recovery", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "show, display", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소방", "en": "firefighting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작업", "en": "work, operation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사고", "en": "accident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당하다", "en": "suffer, be subjected to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "후", "en": "after", "note": ""}, {"ko": "년간", "en": "for ... years", "note": "duration marker"}, {"ko": "깊다", "en": "deep", "note": ""}, {"ko": "혼수상태", "en": "coma", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨어나다", "en": "wake up, come to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": ""}, {"ko": "친구", "en": "friend", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알아보다", "en": "recognize", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "exceed, go over", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during, for (duration)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "최소의식상태", "en": "minimally conscious state", "note": "medical term"}, {"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완전하다", "en": "complete, perfect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기대하다", "en": "expect, hope for", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "difficult, hard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기적", "en": "miracle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "happen, occur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완전히", "en": "completely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "되찾다", "en": "regain, get back", "note": ""}, {"ko": "첫 번째", "en": "first", "note": "ordinal number"}, {"ko": "질문", "en": "question", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아내", "en": "wife", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "formal past tense ending. 보이다 (show) → 보였다 → 보였습니다", "ex_ko": "미국의 소방관 도널드 허버트가 놀라운 회복을 보였습니다.", "ex_en": "American firefighter Donald Herbert showed an amazing recovery."}, {"name": "~중", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "in the middle of, during. 작업 (work) + 중 = during work", "ex_ko": "그는 소방 작업 중 사고를 당해 의식을 잃었어요.", "ex_en": "He lost consciousness in an accident during firefighting work."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "cause/sequence connector. 당하다 → 당해서 → 당해 (contracted). Shows the accident happened and as a result he lost consciousness", "ex_ko": "그는 소방 작업 중 사고를 당해 의식을 잃었어요.", "ex_en": "He lost consciousness in an accident during firefighting work."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past polite ending: 되찾다 → 되찾았어요 (regained).", "ex_ko": "그는 소방 작업 중 사고를 당해 의식을 잃었어요.", "ex_en": "He lost consciousness in an accident during firefighting work."}, {"name": "~에 빠지다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "fall into a state. Used with abstract states like 혼수상태 (coma), 절망 (despair)", "ex_ko": "사고 후 그는 1년간 깊은 혼수상태에 빠졌습니다.", "ex_en": "After the accident, he fell into a deep coma for one year."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은 후에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "after V-ing. 깨어나다 → 깨어난 + 후에 = after waking up", "ex_ko": "깨어난 후에도 가족이나 친구들을 알아보지 못했어요.", "ex_en": "Even after waking up, he couldn''t recognize family or friends."}, {"name": "~에도", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "even (at/to). Shows contrast - even after waking up, still couldn''t recognize", "ex_ko": "깨어난 후에도 가족이나 친구들을 알아보지 못했어요.", "ex_en": "Even after waking up, he couldn''t recognize family or friends."}, {"name": "~(이)나", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "or, choice between options. 가족이나 친구들 = family or friends", "ex_ko": "깨어난 후에도 가족이나 친구들을 알아보지 못했어요.", "ex_en": "Even after waking up, he couldn''t recognize family or friends."}, {"name": "~지 못하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "cannot, inability. 알아보다 → 알아보지 못하다 = cannot recognize", "ex_ko": "깨어난 후에도 가족이나 친구들을 알아보지 못했어요.", "ex_en": "Even after waking up, he couldn''t recognize family or friends."}, {"name": "~는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "present modifier for verbs. 넘다 → 넘는 (time that exceeds)", "ex_ko": "그 후 9년이 넘는 시간 동안 최소의식상태가 계속되었습니다.", "ex_en": "After that, a minimally conscious state continued for over nine years."}, {"name": "~ 동안", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''for / during (a period)''. 9년이 넘는 시간 동안 = for more than nine years.", "ex_ko": "그 후 9년이 넘는 시간 동안 최소의식상태가 계속되었습니다.", "ex_en": "After that, a minimally conscious state continued for over nine years."}, {"name": "~기 어렵다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "difficult to V. Pattern: V-기 + 어렵다 = hard to do V", "ex_ko": "의사들도 완전한 회복을 기대하기 어려웠어요.", "ex_en": "Even doctors found it difficult to expect a complete recovery."}, {"name": "~도 (even)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''even / also''. 의사들도 = even the doctors.", "ex_ko": "의사들도 완전한 회복을 기대하기 어려웠어요.", "ex_en": "Even doctors found it difficult to expect a complete recovery."}, {"name": "~만에", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "after a duration of time. Shows something happens after a long period. 10년 만에 = after 10 years", "ex_ko": "10년 만에 그가 완전히 의식을 되찾았어요.", "ex_en": "After 10 years, he completely regained consciousness."}, {"name": "~에 대한", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "about, regarding. Adnominal form. 아내에 대한 것 = (thing) about his wife", "ex_ko": "깨어난 후 그의 첫 번째 질문은 아내에 대한 것이었습니다.", "ex_en": "His first question after waking up was about his wife."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mp44i0r27bjj' and md5(translation) = '0a2a8266e08ddd2c9fc1dbd7c90513b7';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There is a special cave in New Zealand. Glowworms live in this cave.", "Glowworms are small insects. They emit light at night. The light shows well because it''s dark inside the cave.", "Many people visit this cave. When you enter the cave, lights twinkle above your head. It''s just like stars in the night sky.", "This glowworm cave is a famous tourist attraction in New Zealand. People come from various countries around the world to see it."], "sentences": [{"text": "뉴질랜드에 특별한 동굴이 있어요.", "translation": "There is a special cave in New Zealand.", "vocab": [{"ko": "뉴질랜드", "en": "New Zealand", "note": "country name"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special, particular", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "동굴", "en": "cave", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "exist, be located", "note": "verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "location marker. Shows where something exists or happens. 뉴질랜드에 (in New Zealand)", "example_in_sentence": "뉴질랜드에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. Marks the grammatical subject. 동굴이 (cave + subject marker)", "example_in_sentence": "동굴이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "present polite ending. 있다 (exist) → 있어요 (exists, polite form)", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 동굴에서는 반딧불이가 살고 있어요.", "translation": "Glowworms live in this cave.", "vocab": [{"ko": "동굴", "en": "cave", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "반딧불이", "en": "glowworm, firefly", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "live, reside", "note": "verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서는", "exp": "에서 (in, where something happens) + 는 (topic): 이 동굴에서는 = in this cave.", "example_in_sentence": "동굴에서는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. 반딧불이가 (glowworms + subject marker)", "example_in_sentence": "반딧불이가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "continuous aspect. Shows ongoing action or state. 살다 (live) → 살고 있다 (is living)", "example_in_sentence": "살고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "exp": "present polite informal ending", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "반딧불이는 작은 벌레예요.", "translation": "Glowworms are small insects.", "vocab": [{"ko": "반딧불이", "en": "glowworm, firefly", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "small, little", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "벌레", "en": "insect, bug", "note": "noun"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. Shows what we''re talking about. 반딧불이는 (as for glowworms)", "example_in_sentence": "반딧불이는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은", "exp": "adjective modifier. 작다 (small) → 작은 (small + modifier) to modify 벌레", "example_in_sentence": "작은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요", "exp": "Polite form of 이다 ''to be'', used after a vowel: 벌레 → 벌레예요 (is an insect).", "example_in_sentence": "벌레예요"}]}, {"text": "이들은 밤에 빛을 내요.", "translation": "They emit light at night.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이들", "en": "these (ones), they", "note": "pronoun"}, {"ko": "밤", "en": "night", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "빛", "en": "light", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "내다", "en": "emit, give off, produce", "note": "verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. 이들은 (as for these ones/they)", "example_in_sentence": "이들은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "time marker. Shows when something happens. 밤에 (at night)", "example_in_sentence": "밤에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "object marker. Shows the direct object. 빛을 (light + object marker)", "example_in_sentence": "빛을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "present polite ending. 내다 (emit) → 내요 (emit, polite form)", "example_in_sentence": "내요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "빛을 내다", "exp": "common collocation meaning ''to emit light'' or ''give off light''", "example_in_sentence": "빛을 내요"}]}, {"text": "동굴 안이 어두워서 빛이 잘 보여요.", "translation": "Because it is dark inside the cave, the light can be seen clearly.", "vocab": [{"ko": 