side + location marker)", "example_in_sentence": "안에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "conditional ''if/when''. 들어가다 (enter) → 들어가면 (when you enter)", "example_in_sentence": "들어가면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Marks where something happens: 머리 위에서 = above your head.", "example_in_sentence": "위에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "subject marker. 빛이 (light + subject marker)", "example_in_sentence": "빛이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "present polite ending. 반짝이다 (twinkle) → 반짝여요 (twinkles, polite form)", "example_in_sentence": "반짝여요"}]}, {"text": "마치 밤하늘의 별 같아요.", "translation": "It''s just like stars in the night sky.", "vocab": [{"ko": "마치", "en": "just like, as if", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "밤하늘", "en": "night sky", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "별", "en": "star", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "same, like", "note": "adjective"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive marker. Shows belonging or relation. 밤하늘의 (of the night sky)", "example_in_sentence": "밤하늘의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요", "exp": "present polite ending. 같다 (be like) → 같아요 (is like, polite form)", "example_in_sentence": "같아요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "마치 ~ 같다", "exp": "common expression meaning ''just like'' or ''as if''. Used for comparisons.", "example_in_sentence": "마치 밤하늘의 별 같아요"}]}, {"text": "이 반딧불이 동굴은 뉴질랜드의 유명한 관광지예요.", "translation": "This glowworm cave is a famous tourist attraction in New Zealand.", "vocab": [{"ko": "반딧불이", "en": "glowworm, firefly", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "동굴", "en": "cave", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "뉴질랜드", "en": "New Zealand", "note": "country name"}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "famous", "note": "adjective"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "topic marker. Shows what we''re talking about. 동굴은 (as for the cave)", "example_in_sentence": "동굴은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive marker. 뉴질랜드의 (of New Zealand)", "example_in_s